, 5452, 558, 666, 428, 7318, 9461, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064051386135728, "compression_ratio": 1.3645833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.1245236512802403e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 9.1, "end": 10.34, "text": " Yeah, it's a massive ecosystem.", "tokens": [50820, 865, 11, 309, 311, 257, 5994, 11311, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064051386135728, "compression_ratio": 1.3645833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.1245236512802403e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 10.34, "end": 16.72, "text": " Right. Like you have tools for web scraping, database querying, API routing, literally whatever you need.", "tokens": [50882, 1779, 13, 1743, 291, 362, 3873, 337, 3670, 43738, 11, 8149, 7083, 1840, 11, 9362, 32722, 11, 3736, 2035, 291, 643, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13064051386135728, "compression_ratio": 1.3645833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.1245236512802403e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 1672, "start": 16.72, "end": 30.08, "text": " But, and this is the wild part, if you try to give your agent access to more than, say, a hundred of them at the same time, it mathematically guarantees the complete cognitive collapse of your system.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 4868, 644, 11, 498, 291, 853, 281, 976, 428, 9461, 2105, 281, 544, 813, 11, 584, 11, 257, 3262, 295, 552, 412, 264, 912, 565, 11, 309, 44003, 32567, 264, 3566, 15605, 15584, 295, 428, 1185, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 4, "seek": 1672, "start": 30.42, "end": 31.619999999999997, "text": " It just grinds to a halt.", "tokens": [51050, 467, 445, 16700, 82, 281, 257, 12479, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 5, "seek": 1672, "start": 31.7, "end": 34.96, "text": " Exactly. And it's this core paradox we're all dealing with right now, right?", "tokens": [51114, 7587, 13, 400, 309, 311, 341, 4965, 26221, 321, 434, 439, 6260, 365, 558, 586, 11, 558, 30, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 6, "seek": 1672, "start": 35.0, "end": 37.04, "text": " You're in the trenches of AI development.", "tokens": [51279, 509, 434, 294, 264, 48245, 295, 7318, 3250, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 1672, "start": 37.36, "end": 44.86, "text": " You're trying to make your agent, quote, unquote, smarter by handing it all this procedural knowledge, and you're actually actively lobotomizing its ability to function.", "tokens": [51397, 509, 434, 1382, 281, 652, 428, 9461, 11, 6513, 11, 37557, 11, 20294, 538, 34774, 309, 439, 341, 43951, 3601, 11, 293, 291, 434, 767, 13022, 14366, 42939, 3319, 1080, 3485, 281, 2445, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 1672, "start": 44.92, "end": 45.739999999999995, "text": " Yeah, you're making it worse.", "tokens": [51775, 865, 11, 291, 434, 1455, 309, 5324, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09364218498343851, "compression_ratio": 1.6717791411042944, "no_speech_prob": 5.812238711155882e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 4574, "start": 45.74, "end": 60.06, "text": " So today, for this deep dive, we're looking at why this happens, and more importantly, how this obscure mathematical theory for the 1980s actually holds the secret to fixing the entire architecture of how we build modern agents.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 965, 11, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 11, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 983, 341, 2314, 11, 293, 544, 8906, 11, 577, 341, 34443, 18894, 5261, 337, 264, 13626, 82, 767, 9190, 264, 4054, 281, 19442, 264, 2302, 9482, 295, 577, 321, 1322, 4363, 12554, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05845490003886976, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.0647249141376713e-12}, {"id": 10, "seek": 4574, "start": 60.300000000000004, "end": 67.24000000000001, "text": " It's honestly a phenomenal structural problem because, you know, we've spent the last few years totally obsessing over model weights and parameter counts, right?", "tokens": [51093, 467, 311, 6095, 257, 17778, 15067, 1154, 570, 11, 291, 458, 11, 321, 600, 4418, 264, 1036, 1326, 924, 3879, 35803, 278, 670, 2316, 17443, 293, 13075, 14893, 11, 558, 30, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05845490003886976, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.0647249141376713e-12}, {"id": 11, "seek": 4574, "start": 67.5, "end": 69.94, "text": " Oh, totally. Just bigger models, more data.", "tokens": [51453, 876, 11, 3879, 13, 1449, 3801, 5245, 11, 544, 1412, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05845490003886976, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.0647249141376713e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 6994, "start": 69.94, "end": 78.25999999999999, "text": " Right. But the actual bottleneck we're hitting in deployment today, it isn't the model's inherent intelligence at all. It's the delivery mechanism.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 3539, 44641, 547, 321, 434, 8850, 294, 19317, 965, 11, 309, 1943, 380, 264, 2316, 311, 26387, 7599, 412, 439, 13, 467, 311, 264, 8982, 7513, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09728595293485201, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.489577233261541e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 6994, "start": 78.44, "end": 79.16, "text": " The delivery mechanism.", "tokens": [50790, 440, 8982, 7513, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09728595293485201, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.489577233261541e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 6994, "start": 79.22, "end": 86.1, "text": " Yeah, it's the physical architecture of how we actually hand a piece of knowledge to an active inference session.", "tokens": [50829, 865, 11, 309, 311, 264, 4001, 9482, 295, 577, 321, 767, 1011, 257, 2522, 295, 3601, 281, 364, 4967, 38253, 5481, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09728595293485201, "compression_ratio": 1.5405405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.489577233261541e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 8610, "start": 86.1, "end": 93.86, "text": " Okay, so to get into this, we are synthesizing two distinct but deeply intertwined sources today.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 281, 483, 666, 341, 11, 321, 366, 26617, 3319, 732, 10644, 457, 8760, 44400, 2001, 7139, 965, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534685883340956, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967569706373032e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 8610, "start": 94.11999999999999, "end": 99.02, "text": " The first is a practical engineering framework that came out in July 2026.", "tokens": [50766, 440, 700, 307, 257, 8496, 7043, 8388, 300, 1361, 484, 294, 7370, 945, 10880, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534685883340956, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967569706373032e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 8610, "start": 99.53999999999999, "end": 104.38, "text": " This is by Yin and a team of researchers, and they call it the At Skills Protocol.", "tokens": [51037, 639, 307, 538, 33254, 293, 257, 1469, 295, 10309, 11, 293, 436, 818, 309, 264, 1711, 27856, 48753, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534685883340956, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967569706373032e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 8610, "start": 104.74, "end": 106.82, "text": " Which is a fantastic piece of engineering.", "tokens": [51297, 3013, 307, 257, 5456, 2522, 295, 7043, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534685883340956, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967569706373032e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 8610, "start": 107.0, "end": 107.63999999999999, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51410, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534685883340956, "compression_ratio": 1.4444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967569706373032e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 10764, "start": 107.64, "end": 112.7, "text": " They basically built this highly effective empirical fix to the bottleneck we're talking about.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1936, 3094, 341, 5405, 4942, 31886, 3191, 281, 264, 44641, 547, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202831858212186, "compression_ratio": 1.4982078853046594, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298431788214218e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 10764, "start": 113.16, "end": 122.14, "text": " But the core of our conversation today revolves around a really fascinating paper published just a month later, so August 2026, by an independent researcher known as Flixion.", "tokens": [50641, 583, 264, 4965, 295, 527, 3761, 965, 47934, 926, 257, 534, 10343, 3035, 6572, 445, 257, 1618, 1780, 11, 370, 6897, 945, 10880, 11, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202831858212186, "compression_ratio": 1.4982078853046594, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298431788214218e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 10764, "start": 122.26, "end": 124.28, "text": " Yeah, Flixion Independent Researcher.", "tokens": [51096, 865, 11, 3235, 970, 313, 40310, 10303, 260, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202831858212186, "compression_ratio": 1.4982078853046594, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298431788214218e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10764, "start": 124.34, "end": 124.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51200, 1779, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202831858212186, "compression_ratio": 1.4982078853046594, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298431788214218e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10764, "start": 124.98, "end": 130.82, "text": " And the paper is titled Availability Before Residency, A Free Theorem Reading of Agent Skill Delivery.", "tokens": [51232, 400, 264, 3035, 307, 19841, 11667, 864, 2310, 4546, 5015, 23343, 11, 316, 11551, 440, 37956, 29766, 295, 27174, 40737, 5831, 8549, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1202831858212186, "compression_ratio": 1.4982078853046594, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298431788214218e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 13082, "start": 130.82, "end": 137.98, "text": " And what Flixion does here is they look at what Yin's team built and say, wait a minute, this isn't just some clever software refactor.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 775, 510, 307, 436, 574, 412, 437, 33254, 311, 1469, 3094, 293, 584, 11, 1699, 257, 3456, 11, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 512, 13494, 4722, 1895, 15104, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11693606425806419, "compression_ratio": 1.4941176470588236, "no_speech_prob": 1.2496583629006963e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 13082, "start": 138.29999999999998, "end": 138.88, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50739, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11693606425806419, "compression_ratio": 1.4941176470588236, "no_speech_prob": 1.2496583629006963e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 13082, "start": 139.01999999999998, "end": 145.16, "text": " Like you engineers stumble blindly into a fundamental boundary of type theory that we've known about since, what, 1983?", "tokens": [50775, 1743, 291, 11955, 41302, 47744, 666, 257, 8088, 12866, 295, 2010, 5261, 300, 321, 600, 2570, 466, 1670, 11, 437, 11, 31758, 30, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11693606425806419, "compression_ratio": 1.4941176470588236, "no_speech_prob": 1.2496583629006963e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 13082, "start": 145.54, "end": 146.23999999999998, "text": " Yeah, 1983.", "tokens": [51101, 865, 11, 31758, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11693606425806419, "compression_ratio": 1.4941176470588236, "no_speech_prob": 1.2496583629006963e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 13082, "start": 146.66, "end": 151.44, "text": " And Flixion's paper does something that is just really rare in computer science literature today.", "tokens": [51157, 400, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 3035, 775, 746, 300, 307, 445, 534, 5892, 294, 3820, 3497, 10394, 965, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11693606425806419, "compression_ratio": 1.4941176470588236, "no_speech_prob": 1.2496583629006963e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 15144, "start": 151.44, "end": 163.57999999999998, "text": " I mean, it takes an immediate, highly pragmatic engineering headache, which is prompt exhaustion in LLM agents, and proves that it's merely a symptom of a much deeper, older mathematical pathology.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 309, 2516, 364, 11629, 11, 5405, 46904, 7043, 23520, 11, 597, 307, 12391, 47408, 294, 441, 43, 44, 12554, 11, 293, 25019, 300, 309, 311, 17003, 257, 29370, 295, 257, 709, 7731, 11, 4906, 18894, 3100, 1793, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883875066583807, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895748480167614e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 15144, "start": 163.7, "end": 164.82, "text": " Which is just so cool.", "tokens": [50978, 3013, 307, 445, 370, 1627, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883875066583807, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895748480167614e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 15144, "start": 164.92, "end": 165.34, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51039, 467, 307, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883875066583807, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895748480167614e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 15144, "start": 165.52, "end": 175.6, "text": " Because it forces us to look at the interface of an AI agent, not as this, you know, new frontier of magic, but as a rigid system governed by strict relational parametricity.", "tokens": [51069, 1436, 309, 5874, 505, 281, 574, 412, 264, 9226, 295, 364, 7318, 9461, 11, 406, 382, 341, 11, 291, 458, 11, 777, 35853, 295, 5585, 11, 457, 382, 257, 22195, 1185, 35529, 538, 10910, 38444, 6220, 17475, 507, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08883875066583807, "compression_ratio": 1.5402298850574712, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895748480167614e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 17560, "start": 175.6, "end": 189.16, "text": " Okay, so if you are listening to this, whether you are actively writing deployment scripts, or maybe managing a local set of autonomous tools, or honestly just trying to get a commercial coding assistant to stop hallucinating your API keys.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 291, 366, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 1968, 291, 366, 13022, 3579, 19317, 23294, 11, 420, 1310, 11642, 257, 2654, 992, 295, 23797, 3873, 11, 420, 6095, 445, 1382, 281, 483, 257, 6841, 17720, 10994, 281, 1590, 35212, 8205, 428, 9362, 9317, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 17560, "start": 189.24, "end": 190.12, "text": " We have all been there.", "tokens": [51047, 492, 362, 439, 668, 456, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 17560, "start": 190.35999999999999, "end": 190.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51103, 1779, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 17560, "start": 190.92, "end": 192.62, "text": " You are dealing with this pathology right now.", "tokens": [51131, 509, 366, 6260, 365, 341, 3100, 1793, 558, 586, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 17560, "start": 193.14, "end": 198.18, "text": " So before we can get to the mathematical cure, we really need to carefully dissect the disease.", "tokens": [51242, 407, 949, 321, 393, 483, 281, 264, 18894, 13698, 11, 321, 534, 643, 281, 7500, 48332, 264, 4752, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 17560, "start": 198.38, "end": 202.72, "text": " We have to look at the exact mechanics of how we're breaking our agents today.", "tokens": [51504, 492, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 1900, 12939, 295, 577, 321, 434, 7697, 527, 12554, 965, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10640585213376764, "compression_ratio": 1.6324503311258278, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108453105070144e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 20272, "start": 202.72, "end": 206.85999999999999, "text": " And that all starts with the concept of installing a skill.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 439, 3719, 365, 264, 3410, 295, 20762, 257, 5389, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10955944690075549, "compression_ratio": 1.48068669527897, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899439104362755e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 20272, "start": 207.12, "end": 209.1, "text": " Yeah, that word is doing a lot of damage.", "tokens": [50585, 865, 11, 300, 1349, 307, 884, 257, 688, 295, 4344, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10955944690075549, "compression_ratio": 1.48068669527897, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899439104362755e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 20272, "start": 209.22, "end": 214.78, "text": " If you look at the July 2026 crawl data referenced in the literature, it paints a very stark picture.", "tokens": [50690, 759, 291, 574, 412, 264, 7370, 945, 10880, 24767, 1412, 32734, 294, 264, 10394, 11, 309, 28076, 257, 588, 17417, 3036, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10955944690075549, "compression_ratio": 1.48068669527897, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899439104362755e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 20272, "start": 214.96, "end": 225.57999999999998, "text": " I mean, Yin et al. documented 56,804 distinct agent skills spread across something like 11,133 repositories.", "tokens": [50977, 286, 914, 11, 33254, 1030, 419, 13, 23007, 19687, 11, 4702, 19, 10644, 9461, 3942, 3974, 2108, 746, 411, 2975, 11, 7668, 18, 22283, 2083, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10955944690075549, "compression_ratio": 1.48068669527897, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899439104362755e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 20272, "start": 225.76, "end": 227.44, "text": " That is just a mountain of code.", "tokens": [51517, 663, 307, 445, 257, 6937, 295, 3089, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10955944690075549, "compression_ratio": 1.48068669527897, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899439104362755e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 22744, "start": 227.44, "end": 228.02, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 13, 50394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 22744, "start": 228.24, "end": 234.78, "text": " And in this context, when we say skill, it's typically encapsulated in a procedural markdown file, usually just labeled skill.md.", "tokens": [50405, 400, 294, 341, 4319, 11, 562, 321, 584, 5389, 11, 309, 311, 5850, 38745, 6987, 294, 257, 43951, 1491, 5093, 3991, 11, 2673, 445, 21335, 5389, 13, 76, 67, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 22744, "start": 234.85999999999999, "end": 235.9, "text": " Right, I've seen a million of those.", "tokens": [50736, 1779, 11, 286, 600, 1612, 257, 2459, 295, 729, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 22744, "start": 235.98, "end": 236.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50792, 7587, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 22744, "start": 236.64, "end": 244.72, "text": " And this file contains the explicit step-by-step logic, the API schemas, and the formatting rules required to execute a specific task.", "tokens": [50825, 400, 341, 3991, 8306, 264, 13691, 1823, 12, 2322, 12, 16792, 9952, 11, 264, 9362, 22627, 296, 11, 293, 264, 39366, 4474, 4739, 281, 14483, 257, 2685, 5633, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 22744, "start": 244.82, "end": 246.2, "text": " Basically, it's the instruction manual.", "tokens": [51234, 8537, 11, 309, 311, 264, 10951, 9688, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310154696305593, "compression_ratio": 1.493723849372385, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992393619293274e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 24620, "start": 246.2, "end": 253.94, "text": " And the default, industry-standard way to give that manual to an agent is to hit an install command.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 7576, 11, 3518, 12, 1115, 515, 636, 281, 976, 300, 9688, 281, 364, 9461, 307, 281, 2045, 364, 3625, 5622, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13345817724863687, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494652664937766e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 24620, "start": 254.82, "end": 262.52, "text": " But Yin's team points out that this word install is doing a massive amount of hidden, completely unacknowledged heavy lifting.", "tokens": [50796, 583, 33254, 311, 1469, 2793, 484, 300, 341, 1349, 3625, 307, 884, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 7633, 11, 2584, 517, 501, 3785, 1493, 3004, 4676, 15798, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13345817724863687, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494652664937766e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 24620, "start": 262.96, "end": 264.82, "text": " It's a completely overloaded verb.", "tokens": [51203, 467, 311, 257, 2584, 28777, 292, 9595, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13345817724863687, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494652664937766e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 24620, "start": 264.96, "end": 265.71999999999997, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51303, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13345817724863687, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.2494652664937766e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 26572, "start": 265.72, "end": 275.90000000000003, "text": " When you trigger an installation in a standard agent framework, you are actually forcing the system to execute three entirely distinct operations, and they're permanently bundled together.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 7875, 364, 13260, 294, 257, 3832, 9461, 8388, 11, 291, 366, 767, 19030, 264, 1185, 281, 14483, 1045, 7696, 10644, 7705, 11, 293, 436, 434, 24042, 13882, 1493, 1214, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 26572, "start": 276.02000000000004, "end": 277.8, "text": " Right, which is the root of the issue.", "tokens": [50880, 1779, 11, 597, 307, 264, 5593, 295, 264, 2734, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 26572, "start": 277.86, "end": 278.0, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50972, 865, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 26572, "start": 278.1, "end": 281.76000000000005, "text": " So first, you're telling the system to fetch the raw content from the remote repository.", "tokens": [50984, 407, 700, 11, 291, 434, 3585, 264, 1185, 281, 23673, 264, 8936, 2701, 490, 264, 8607, 25841, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 26572, "start": 282.46000000000004, "end": 286.08000000000004, "text": " Second, you are telling it to vendor a local copy onto your disk.", "tokens": [51202, 5736, 11, 291, 366, 3585, 309, 281, 24321, 257, 2654, 5055, 3911, 428, 12355, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 26572, "start": 286.42, "end": 291.92, "text": " And third, and this is the crucial one, you are demanding that the skill be enabled for auto-triggering.", "tokens": [51400, 400, 2636, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 11462, 472, 11, 291, 366, 19960, 300, 264, 5389, 312, 15172, 337, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11450643375002105, "compression_ratio": 1.7298245614035088, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325133960990666e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 29192, "start": 291.92, "end": 292.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 29192, "start": 293.02000000000004, "end": 296.86, "text": " That third operation is exactly where the architecture begins to fracture.", "tokens": [50420, 663, 2636, 6916, 307, 2293, 689, 264, 9482, 7338, 281, 36877, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 29192, "start": 297.36, "end": 302.88, "text": " Because, think about it, auto-triggering requires the agent to be continuously aware that the skill exists.", "tokens": [50637, 1436, 11, 519, 466, 309, 11, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 7029, 264, 9461, 281, 312, 15684, 3650, 300, 264, 5389, 8198, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 29192, "start": 302.96000000000004, "end": 303.58000000000004, "text": " At all times.", "tokens": [50917, 1711, 439, 1413, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 29192, "start": 303.7, "end": 304.46000000000004, "text": " At all times.", "tokens": [50954, 1711, 439, 1413, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 29192, "start": 304.54, "end": 310.86, "text": " It has to know what its parameters are and under what semantic conditions it should be invoked, even when the user hasn't explicitly asked for it.", "tokens": [50996, 467, 575, 281, 458, 437, 1080, 9834, 366, 293, 833, 437, 47982, 4487, 309, 820, 312, 1048, 9511, 11, 754, 562, 264, 4195, 6132, 380, 20803, 2351, 337, 309, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 29192, "start": 310.86, "end": 320.62, "text": " Right, so to achieve that continuous awareness, the framework has to physically inject the front-matter description of that skill.md file directly into the agent's system prompt.", "tokens": [51312, 1779, 11, 370, 281, 4584, 300, 10957, 8888, 11, 264, 8388, 575, 281, 9762, 10711, 264, 1868, 12, 76, 1161, 3855, 295, 300, 5389, 13, 76, 67, 3991, 3838, 666, 264, 9461, 311, 1185, 12391, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 29192, "start": 320.8, "end": 321.58000000000004, "text": " Which is expensive.", "tokens": [51809, 3013, 307, 5124, 13, 51848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1246265755560165, "compression_ratio": 1.6948640483383686, "no_speech_prob": 1.9728992745049467e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 32158, "start": 321.58, "end": 322.52, "text": " And super expensive.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1687, 5124, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 32158, "start": 322.62, "end": 322.8, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50417, 865, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 32158, "start": 322.94, "end": 327.82, "text": " It has to sit right there in the immediate context window for every single inference term.", "tokens": [50433, 467, 575, 281, 1394, 558, 456, 294, 264, 11629, 4319, 4910, 337, 633, 2167, 38253, 1433, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 32158, "start": 329.03999999999996, "end": 331.85999999999996, "text": " Which brings us to the literature on positional attention.", "tokens": [50738, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 10394, 322, 2535, 304, 3202, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 32158, "start": 332.68, "end": 340.44, "text": " The paper cites some foundational work from 2024 and 2025 by Lou Laban and Jaslavic.", "tokens": [50920, 440, 3035, 269, 3324, 512, 32195, 589, 490, 45237, 293, 39209, 538, 7272, 10137, 282, 293, 34023, 36243, 299, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 32158, "start": 340.64, "end": 341.94, "text": " Right, a really important study.", "tokens": [51318, 1779, 11, 257, 534, 1021, 2979, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 32158, "start": 342.02, "end": 342.15999999999997, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51387, 865, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 32158, "start": 342.41999999999996, "end": 347.79999999999995, "text": " Let's dig into their findings, because they map out exactly why shoving everything into the system prompt is just a fatal error.", "tokens": [51407, 961, 311, 2528, 666, 641, 16483, 11, 570, 436, 4471, 484, 2293, 983, 2223, 798, 1203, 666, 264, 1185, 12391, 307, 445, 257, 24069, 6713, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16653269473637375, "compression_ratio": 1.5376344086021505, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351779293602656e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 34780, "start": 347.8, "end": 356.0, "text": " So those researchers conducted expensive empirical studies on how transformer architectures actually allocate attention across long context windows.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 729, 10309, 13809, 5124, 31886, 5313, 322, 577, 31782, 6331, 1303, 767, 35713, 3202, 2108, 938, 4319, 9309, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13621708498162738, "compression_ratio": 1.4646464646464648, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881594863335514e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 34780, "start": 356.2, "end": 361.88, "text": " Because, you know, the marketing materials for modern LLMs love to tell these windows of a million tokens or more.", "tokens": [50785, 1436, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 6370, 5319, 337, 4363, 441, 43, 26386, 959, 281, 980, 613, 9309, 295, 257, 2459, 22667, 420, 544, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13621708498162738, "compression_ratio": 1.4646464646464648, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881594863335514e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 34780, "start": 362.02000000000004, "end": 363.24, "text": " Oh yeah, infinite concept.", "tokens": [51076, 876, 1338, 11, 13785, 3410, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13621708498162738, "compression_ratio": 1.4646464646464648, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881594863335514e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 36324, "start": 363.24, "end": 367.52, "text": " Exactly, implying this vast, perfectly reliable working memory.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 11, 704, 7310, 341, 8369, 11, 6239, 12924, 1364, 4675, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3452991843223572, "compression_ratio": 0.9402985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232430980964163e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 36752, "start": 367.52, "end": 384.62, "text": " But Lou Laban and Jaslavic prove that while a model can technically, physically ingest a million tokens, its ability to reliably extract and execute discrete procedural instructions from that context decays non-linearly.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 7272, 10137, 282, 293, 34023, 36243, 299, 7081, 300, 1339, 257, 2316, 393, 12120, 11, 9762, 3957, 377, 257, 2459, 22667, 11, 1080, 3485, 281, 49927, 8947, 293, 14483, 27706, 43951, 9415, 490, 300, 4319, 979, 3772, 2107, 12, 28263, 356, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13010848836695893, "compression_ratio": 1.3924050632911393, "no_speech_prob": 2.043944440782708e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 38462, "start": 384.62, "end": 386.56, "text": " The whole loss in the middle phenomena.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1379, 4470, 294, 264, 2808, 22004, 13, 50462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 38462, "start": 386.68, "end": 387.12, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50468, 48746, 736, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 38462, "start": 387.28000000000003, "end": 389.76, "text": " The attention heads basically get spread too thin.", "tokens": [50498, 440, 3202, 8050, 1936, 483, 3974, 886, 5862, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 38462, "start": 389.9, "end": 390.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50629, 1779, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 38462, "start": 390.18, "end": 400.0, "text": " So if you load up the context with dozens of disparate, completely unconnected instructional frames, the model's attention matrix degrades into just this uniform blur.", "tokens": [50643, 407, 498, 291, 3677, 493, 264, 4319, 365, 18431, 295, 14548, 473, 11, 2584, 517, 9826, 292, 35716, 12083, 11, 264, 2316, 311, 3202, 8141, 368, 22626, 666, 445, 341, 9452, 14257, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 38462, "start": 400.36, "end": 405.3, "text": " It loses the sharp activation spikes that it actually needs to execute specific logic.", "tokens": [51152, 467, 18293, 264, 8199, 24433, 28997, 300, 309, 767, 2203, 281, 14483, 2685, 9952, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 38462, "start": 405.48, "end": 406.42, "text": " It just washes out.", "tokens": [51408, 467, 445, 48616, 484, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 38462, "start": 406.62, "end": 406.82, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51465, 865, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 38462, "start": 406.82, "end": 414.08, "text": " And the literature consensus suggests that once you cross a threshold of fewer than 100 reliable instruction slots, the context begins to collapse.", "tokens": [51475, 400, 264, 10394, 19115, 13409, 300, 1564, 291, 3278, 257, 14678, 295, 13366, 813, 2319, 12924, 10951, 24266, 11, 264, 4319, 7338, 281, 15584, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374439395842005, "compression_ratio": 1.6422018348623852, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716290654090088e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 41408, "start": 414.08, "end": 416.53999999999996, "text": " Fewer than 100 out of 56,000 available.", "tokens": [50365, 33468, 260, 813, 2319, 484, 295, 19687, 11, 1360, 2435, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 41408, "start": 416.68, "end": 416.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50495, 1779, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 41408, "start": 417.03999999999996, "end": 420.88, "text": " And so the agent starts skipping steps or it starts blending the rules of two different skills together.", "tokens": [50513, 400, 370, 264, 9461, 3719, 31533, 4439, 420, 309, 3719, 23124, 264, 4474, 295, 732, 819, 3942, 1214, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 41408, "start": 421.0, "end": 421.12, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50711, 865, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 41408, "start": 421.3, "end": 425.46, "text": " Or it just defaults to whatever instruction happened to be placed at the very, very end of the prompt.", "tokens": [50726, 1610, 309, 445, 7576, 82, 281, 2035, 10951, 2011, 281, 312, 7074, 412, 264, 588, 11, 588, 917, 295, 264, 12391, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 41408, "start": 425.74, "end": 426.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50948, 7587, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 41408, "start": 426.38, "end": 438.21999999999997, "text": " So you have this theoretical universe of 56,804 available skills, but a strict physical constraint of fewer than 100 residency slots in the attention mechanism.", "tokens": [50980, 407, 291, 362, 341, 20864, 6445, 295, 19687, 11, 4702, 19, 2435, 3942, 11, 457, 257, 10910, 4001, 25534, 295, 13366, 813, 2319, 34014, 24266, 294, 264, 3202, 7513, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12641100700084978, "compression_ratio": 1.5808823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276379537719324e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 43822, "start": 438.22, "end": 445.52000000000004, "text": " If you bundle the act of obtaining a skill with the requirement that it physically reside in the prompt, you hit a hard and flexible ceiling.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 24438, 264, 605, 295, 36749, 257, 5389, 365, 264, 11695, 300, 309, 9762, 40134, 294, 264, 12391, 11, 291, 2045, 257, 1152, 293, 11358, 13655, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071809060645826, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 43822, "start": 446.06, "end": 451.72, "text": " And this creates an immediate highly toxic resource competition, especially in enterprise environments.", "tokens": [50757, 400, 341, 7829, 364, 11629, 5405, 12786, 7684, 6211, 11, 2318, 294, 14132, 12388, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071809060645826, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 43822, "start": 451.82000000000005, "end": 453.90000000000003, "text": " If you think about your own team's private workflow.", "tokens": [51045, 759, 291, 519, 466, 428, 1065, 1469, 311, 4551, 20993, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071809060645826, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 43822, "start": 454.16, "end": 454.42, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51162, 1779, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071809060645826, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879033977804103e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 45442, "start": 454.42, "end": 463.28000000000003, "text": " You have highly specific mission-critical procedures like your internal CICD deployment routing or specific database sanitization rules.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 5405, 2685, 4447, 12, 32255, 804, 13846, 411, 428, 6920, 383, 2532, 35, 19317, 32722, 420, 2685, 8149, 24533, 2144, 4474, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1055738488022162, "compression_ratio": 1.5910652920962198, "no_speech_prob": 1.642373845429923e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 45442, "start": 463.92, "end": 472.96000000000004, "text": " If one of your developers installs a dozen helpful public utility skills, say like a meet markdown format or a public web scraper and maybe a generic debugging tool,", "tokens": [50840, 759, 472, 295, 428, 8849, 3625, 82, 257, 16654, 4961, 1908, 14877, 3942, 11, 584, 411, 257, 1677, 1491, 5093, 7877, 420, 257, 1908, 3670, 13943, 610, 293, 1310, 257, 19577, 45592, 2290, 11, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1055738488022162, "compression_ratio": 1.5910652920962198, "no_speech_prob": 1.642373845429923e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 45442, "start": 473.34000000000003, "end": 478.86, "text": " those public tools are suddenly competing for the exact same scarce prompt slots as your core infrastructure logic.", "tokens": [51311, 729, 1908, 3873, 366, 5800, 15439, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 41340, 12391, 24266, 382, 428, 4965, 6896, 9952, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1055738488022162, "compression_ratio": 1.5910652920962198, "no_speech_prob": 1.642373845429923e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 45442, "start": 479.02000000000004, "end": 481.24, "text": " It's a complete architectural zero-sum game.", "tokens": [51595, 467, 311, 257, 3566, 26621, 4018, 12, 82, 449, 1216, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1055738488022162, "compression_ratio": 1.5910652920962198, "no_speech_prob": 1.642373845429923e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 48124, "start": 481.24, "end": 489.16, "text": " It is. If the attention window overflows, the generic public skills might silently push your team's critical deployment protocols right out of the agent's reliable memory.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 13, 759, 264, 3202, 4910, 670, 33229, 11, 264, 19577, 1908, 3942, 1062, 40087, 2944, 428, 1469, 311, 4924, 19317, 20618, 558, 484, 295, 264, 9461, 311, 12924, 4675, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09085916555844821, "compression_ratio": 1.632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.83980955470453e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 48124, "start": 489.34000000000003, "end": 491.34000000000003, "text": " Which is terrifying for a production system.", "tokens": [50770, 3013, 307, 18106, 337, 257, 4265, 1185, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09085916555844821, "compression_ratio": 1.632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.83980955470453e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 48124, "start": 491.92, "end": 496.68, "text": " Every skill you install dilutes the model's ability to focus on the skills it already has.", "tokens": [50899, 2048, 5389, 291, 3625, 11504, 1819, 264, 2316, 311, 3485, 281, 1879, 322, 264, 3942, 309, 1217, 575, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09085916555844821, "compression_ratio": 1.632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.83980955470453e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 48124, "start": 497.2, "end": 505.58, "text": " The model is essentially forced to constantly evaluate the relevance of tools it isn't currently using, which exhausts its cognitive capacity.", "tokens": [51163, 440, 2316, 307, 4476, 7579, 281, 6460, 13059, 264, 32684, 295, 3873, 309, 1943, 380, 4362, 1228, 11, 597, 14687, 82, 1080, 15605, 6042, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09085916555844821, "compression_ratio": 1.632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.83980955470453e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 48124, "start": 505.96000000000004, "end": 507.40000000000003, "text": " I always compare it to a backpack.", "tokens": [51601, 286, 1009, 6794, 309, 281, 257, 17969, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09085916555844821, "compression_ratio": 1.632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.83980955470453e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 50740, "start": 507.4, "end": 513.4399999999999, "text": " It's like forcing someone to carry a hundred heavy tools in their backpack at all times just in case they need one, right?", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 19030, 1580, 281, 3985, 257, 3262, 4676, 3873, 294, 641, 17969, 412, 439, 1413, 445, 294, 1389, 436, 643, 472, 11, 558, 30, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1066044428015268, "compression_ratio": 1.6016260162601625, "no_speech_prob": 2.075677520488317e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 50740, "start": 514.04, "end": 518.64, "text": " Instead of just leaving the tools in a garage and reading the manual when a specific job arises.", "tokens": [50697, 7156, 295, 445, 5012, 264, 3873, 294, 257, 14400, 293, 3760, 264, 9688, 562, 257, 2685, 1691, 27388, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1066044428015268, "compression_ratio": 1.6016260162601625, "no_speech_prob": 2.075677520488317e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 50740, "start": 518.8, "end": 520.1, "text": " That's a perfect analogy.", "tokens": [50935, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 21663, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1066044428015268, "compression_ratio": 1.6016260162601625, "no_speech_prob": 2.075677520488317e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 50740, "start": 520.26, "end": 529.22, "text": " Or it's like taking a standard executable file and deciding that the only way to ship it is to bundle it inside an entire bootable virtual OS image.", "tokens": [51008, 1610, 309, 311, 411, 1940, 257, 3832, 7568, 712, 3991, 293, 17990, 300, 264, 787, 636, 281, 5374, 309, 307, 281, 24438, 309, 1854, 364, 2302, 11450, 712, 6374, 12731, 3256, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1066044428015268, "compression_ratio": 1.6016260162601625, "no_speech_prob": 2.075677520488317e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 52922, "start": 529.22, "end": 538.28, "text": " You aren't just passing the necessary data, you're forcing the receiving system to spin up massive amounts of computational overhead just to read a simple string of text.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 3212, 380, 445, 8437, 264, 4818, 1412, 11, 291, 434, 19030, 264, 10040, 1185, 281, 6060, 493, 5994, 11663, 295, 28270, 19922, 445, 281, 1401, 257, 2199, 6798, 295, 2487, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057535457611084, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043178733254668e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 52922, "start": 538.6800000000001, "end": 545.0600000000001, "text": " We're basically forcing the agent to carry the metadata of every single tool in his active working memory at all times.", "tokens": [50838, 492, 434, 1936, 19030, 264, 9461, 281, 3985, 264, 26603, 295, 633, 2167, 2290, 294, 702, 4967, 1364, 4675, 412, 439, 1413, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057535457611084, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043178733254668e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 52922, "start": 545.2, "end": 550.38, "text": " Which is why Yin et al. recognized that this was a deeply inefficient bundling of features.", "tokens": [51164, 3013, 307, 983, 33254, 1030, 419, 13, 9823, 300, 341, 390, 257, 8760, 43495, 13882, 1688, 295, 4122, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057535457611084, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043178733254668e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 52922, "start": 550.82, "end": 553.96, "text": " And so they designed an alternative, which is the at-skills protocol.", "tokens": [51445, 400, 370, 436, 4761, 364, 8535, 11, 597, 307, 264, 412, 12, 5161, 2565, 10336, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1057535457611084, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043178733254668e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 55396, "start": 553.96, "end": 559.12, "text": " Right. So let's look at Yin's solution before diving into the deep math that explains why it works.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 407, 718, 311, 574, 412, 33254, 311, 3827, 949, 20241, 666, 264, 2452, 5221, 300, 13948, 983, 309, 1985, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 55396, "start": 560.1800000000001, "end": 565.26, "text": " The at-skills protocol is essentially this exercise in aggressive unbundling.", "tokens": [50676, 440, 412, 12, 5161, 2565, 10336, 307, 4476, 341, 5380, 294, 10762, 517, 65, 997, 1688, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 55396, "start": 565.34, "end": 566.26, "text": " Highly aggressive.", "tokens": [50934, 5229, 356, 10762, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 55396, "start": 566.5400000000001, "end": 569.2, "text": " Yin and their team looked at the install paradigm.", "tokens": [50994, 33254, 293, 641, 1469, 2956, 412, 264, 3625, 24709, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 55396, "start": 569.36, "end": 571.26, "text": " They looked at the positional attention bottleneck.", "tokens": [51135, 814, 2956, 412, 264, 2535, 304, 3202, 44641, 547, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 55396, "start": 571.62, "end": 576.74, "text": " And they decided to shatter the installation process into three distinct isolated tiers.", "tokens": [51248, 400, 436, 3047, 281, 402, 1161, 264, 13260, 1399, 666, 1045, 10644, 14621, 40563, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 55396, "start": 577.1, "end": 583.0600000000001, "text": " And these are based on what actually incurs a token cost and what genuinely triggers reliably in an LLM.", "tokens": [51522, 400, 613, 366, 2361, 322, 437, 767, 834, 2156, 257, 14862, 2063, 293, 437, 17839, 22827, 49927, 294, 364, 441, 43, 44, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10749322125035474, "compression_ratio": 1.7058823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977308873652232e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 58306, "start": 583.06, "end": 583.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 58306, "start": 584.06, "end": 587.02, "text": " Let's walk through those piers, starting with Tier 1, the bare reference.", "tokens": [50415, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 729, 3895, 433, 11, 2891, 365, 24224, 502, 11, 264, 6949, 6408, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 58306, "start": 587.3199999999999, "end": 589.3399999999999, "text": " This is the foundation of the whole unbundling thing.", "tokens": [50578, 639, 307, 264, 7030, 295, 264, 1379, 517, 65, 997, 1688, 551, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 58306, "start": 589.8599999999999, "end": 592.0999999999999, "text": " In Tier 1, there is no installation step at all.", "tokens": [50705, 682, 24224, 502, 11, 456, 307, 572, 13260, 1823, 412, 439, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 58306, "start": 592.4799999999999, "end": 597.8599999999999, "text": " You simply type a path like at Giddy Veserbolskil directly into your chat message to the agent.", "tokens": [50836, 509, 2935, 2010, 257, 3100, 411, 412, 460, 327, 3173, 691, 279, 260, 17460, 5161, 388, 3838, 666, 428, 5081, 3636, 281, 264, 9461, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 58306, "start": 598.6999999999999, "end": 603.18, "text": " So what is happening architecturally under the hood when a user does that?", "tokens": [51147, 407, 437, 307, 2737, 6331, 6512, 833, 264, 13376, 562, 257, 4195, 775, 300, 30, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 58306, "start": 603.28, "end": 608.9399999999999, "text": " Okay. So when the agent's orchestration layer encounters that bare reference, it halts the standard inference cycle.", "tokens": [51376, 1033, 13, 407, 562, 264, 9461, 311, 14161, 2405, 4583, 26310, 300, 6949, 6408, 11, 309, 7523, 1373, 264, 3832, 38253, 6586, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 58306, "start": 609.06, "end": 609.66, "text": " It just stops.", "tokens": [51665, 467, 445, 10094, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20590476102607194, "compression_ratio": 1.6212624584717608, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945026111436778e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 60966, "start": 609.66, "end": 618.76, "text": " Then it resolves that network path, fetches the raw markdown content of the skill, and injects it exactly at the point of execution within that specific message turn.", "tokens": [50365, 1396, 309, 7923, 977, 300, 3209, 3100, 11, 15136, 3781, 264, 8936, 1491, 5093, 2701, 295, 264, 5389, 11, 293, 10711, 82, 309, 2293, 412, 264, 935, 295, 15058, 1951, 300, 2685, 3636, 1261, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12269102560507285, "compression_ratio": 1.5665024630541873, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324679881137618e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 60966, "start": 618.92, "end": 622.12, "text": " So it's basically just-in-time dependency resolution.", "tokens": [50828, 407, 309, 311, 1936, 445, 12, 259, 12, 3766, 33621, 8669, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12269102560507285, "compression_ratio": 1.5665024630541873, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324679881137618e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 60966, "start": 622.26, "end": 624.4399999999999, "text": " Essentially a JIT dependency resolution, yes.", "tokens": [50995, 23596, 257, 508, 3927, 33621, 8669, 11, 2086, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12269102560507285, "compression_ratio": 1.5665024630541873, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324679881137618e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 60966, "start": 624.62, "end": 627.4399999999999, "text": " But here is the critical architectural distinction.", "tokens": [51113, 583, 510, 307, 264, 4924, 26621, 16844, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12269102560507285, "compression_ratio": 1.5665024630541873, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324679881137618e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 62744, "start": 627.44, "end": 635.74, "text": " Once that specific inference turn is complete, the context window collapses back to its baseline state.", "tokens": [50365, 3443, 300, 2685, 38253, 1261, 307, 3566, 11, 264, 4319, 4910, 48765, 646, 281, 1080, 20518, 1785, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15849931616532176, "compression_ratio": 1.391812865497076, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111275283325123e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 62744, "start": 635.86, "end": 636.3800000000001, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50786, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15849931616532176, "compression_ratio": 1.391812865497076, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111275283325123e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 62744, "start": 636.58, "end": 636.7600000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50822, 865, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15849931616532176, "compression_ratio": 1.391812865497076, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111275283325123e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 62744, "start": 636.9000000000001, "end": 638.9000000000001, "text": " The fetched skill is garbage collected.", "tokens": [50838, 440, 23673, 292, 5389, 307, 14150, 11087, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15849931616532176, "compression_ratio": 1.391812865497076, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111275283325123e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 62744, "start": 639.32, "end": 643.96, "text": " It leaves absolutely no standing memory footprint in the ongoing system prompt.", "tokens": [50959, 467, 5510, 3122, 572, 4877, 4675, 24222, 294, 264, 10452, 1185, 12391, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15849931616532176, "compression_ratio": 1.391812865497076, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111275283325123e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 64396, "start": 643.96, "end": 649.0600000000001, "text": " So the standing token cost for having that skill available for your next request is zero.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 4877, 14862, 2063, 337, 1419, 300, 5389, 2435, 337, 428, 958, 5308, 307, 4018, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 64396, "start": 649.3000000000001, "end": 650.0600000000001, "text": " Zero tokens.", "tokens": [50632, 17182, 22667, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 64396, "start": 650.34, "end": 651.14, "text": " That's incredible.", "tokens": [50684, 663, 311, 4651, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 64396, "start": 651.26, "end": 659.24, "text": " You bypass the prompt limitation entirely because you only pay the token cost precisely at the millisecond you are actively invoking the tool.", "tokens": [50730, 509, 24996, 264, 12391, 27432, 7696, 570, 291, 787, 1689, 264, 14862, 2063, 13402, 412, 264, 27940, 18882, 291, 366, 13022, 1048, 5953, 264, 2290, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 64396, "start": 659.4200000000001, "end": 659.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51138, 7587, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 64396, "start": 660.4000000000001, "end": 666.6, "text": " But Yin's team also recognized that pulling from a remote repository on every single turn isn't always practical.", "tokens": [51187, 583, 33254, 311, 1469, 611, 9823, 300, 8407, 490, 257, 8607, 25841, 322, 633, 2167, 1261, 1943, 380, 1009, 8496, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531351133324634, "compression_ratio": 1.560483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 1.617306549100972e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 66660, "start": 666.6, "end": 671.4, "text": " I mean, you have network latency, versioning instability, maybe offline development environments.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 291, 362, 3209, 27043, 11, 3037, 278, 34379, 11, 1310, 21857, 3250, 12388, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 66660, "start": 671.44, "end": 671.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50607, 1779, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 66660, "start": 671.58, "end": 673.48, "text": " You can't always rely on an external ping.", "tokens": [50614, 509, 393, 380, 1009, 10687, 322, 364, 8320, 26151, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 66660, "start": 673.66, "end": 674.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50718, 7587, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 66660, "start": 674.44, "end": 677.1800000000001, "text": " So that brings us to tier two, the saved copy.", "tokens": [50757, 407, 300, 5607, 505, 281, 12362, 732, 11, 264, 6624, 5055, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 66660, "start": 677.6, "end": 682.2, "text": " In this tier, the skill is vendored into your project's local Git-tracked file tree.", "tokens": [50915, 682, 341, 12362, 11, 264, 5389, 307, 10169, 2769, 666, 428, 1716, 311, 2654, 16939, 12, 19466, 292, 3991, 4230, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 66660, "start": 682.5, "end": 682.74, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51160, 1033, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 66660, "start": 682.82, "end": 684.4200000000001, "text": " So this is a localized dependency.", "tokens": [51176, 407, 341, 307, 257, 44574, 33621, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 66660, "start": 684.58, "end": 687.76, "text": " You're pulling the skill.md file down to your local hard drive.", "tokens": [51264, 509, 434, 8407, 264, 5389, 13, 76, 67, 3991, 760, 281, 428, 2654, 1152, 3332, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 66660, "start": 688.16, "end": 690.22, "text": " But again, where is this file indexed?", "tokens": [51443, 583, 797, 11, 689, 307, 341, 3991, 8186, 292, 30, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 66660, "start": 690.26, "end": 694.52, "text": " It is indexed entirely by your external non-LLM tooling.", "tokens": [51548, 467, 307, 8186, 292, 7696, 538, 428, 8320, 2107, 12, 24010, 44, 46593, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 66660, "start": 694.6800000000001, "end": 695.1800000000001, "text": " Ah, okay.", "tokens": [51769, 2438, 11, 1392, 13, 51794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14258294005494018, "compression_ratio": 1.5993589743589745, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895714869900267e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 69518, "start": 695.18, "end": 703.4799999999999, "text": " It sits on disk, it's tracked by Git, it's integrated into your IDE, but it remains completely outside the model's context window.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 12696, 322, 12355, 11, 309, 311, 31703, 538, 16939, 11, 309, 311, 10919, 666, 428, 40930, 11, 457, 309, 7023, 2584, 2380, 264, 2316, 311, 4319, 4910, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 69518, "start": 703.9799999999999, "end": 706.3, "text": " The agent has no passive awareness of it.", "tokens": [50805, 440, 9461, 575, 572, 14975, 8888, 295, 309, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 69518, "start": 706.5799999999999, "end": 709.56, "text": " So if you want to use it, you still have to reference its local path.", "tokens": [50935, 407, 498, 291, 528, 281, 764, 309, 11, 291, 920, 362, 281, 6408, 1080, 2654, 3100, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 69518, "start": 709.64, "end": 709.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51088, 1079, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 69518, "start": 710.5, "end": 714.02, "text": " Therefore, the standing token cost to the prompt remains zero.", "tokens": [51131, 7504, 11, 264, 4877, 14862, 2063, 281, 264, 12391, 7023, 4018, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 69518, "start": 714.5799999999999, "end": 718.62, "text": " The prompt is perfectly protected from the sheer volume of your saved skills.", "tokens": [51335, 440, 12391, 307, 6239, 10594, 490, 264, 23061, 5523, 295, 428, 6624, 3942, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 69518, "start": 718.8199999999999, "end": 722.56, "text": " Which brings us to the final piece of the puzzle, tier three, the installed line.", "tokens": [51547, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 2522, 295, 264, 12805, 11, 12362, 1045, 11, 264, 8899, 1622, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12862736139542016, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496179864126324e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 72256, "start": 722.56, "end": 727.4, "text": " This is the only mechanism in the entire AdSkills protocol that touches the system prompt.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 787, 7513, 294, 264, 2302, 1999, 50, 74, 2565, 10336, 300, 17431, 264, 1185, 12391, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10979618745691636, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234770689252387e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 72256, "start": 727.6199999999999, "end": 731.64, "text": " And you only invoke tier three when you're purchasing one very specific property, right?", "tokens": [50618, 400, 291, 787, 41117, 12362, 1045, 562, 291, 434, 20906, 472, 588, 2685, 4707, 11, 558, 30, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10979618745691636, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234770689252387e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 72256, "start": 731.8599999999999, "end": 732.0999999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50830, 1079, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10979618745691636, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234770689252387e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 72256, "start": 732.3, "end": 737.26, "text": " The ability for the agent to auto-trigger the skill without the user explicitly naming the path.", "tokens": [50852, 440, 3485, 337, 264, 9461, 281, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 264, 5389, 1553, 264, 4195, 20803, 25290, 264, 3100, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10979618745691636, "compression_ratio": 1.4712041884816753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234770689252387e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 73726, "start": 737.26, "end": 737.8, "text": " That's right.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 558, 13, 50392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16447540231653163, "compression_ratio": 1.504950495049505, "no_speech_prob": 1.1737641024064938e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 73726, "start": 738.34, "end": 742.8199999999999, "text": " When you promote a skill to tier three, the protocol generates a dot auto-trigger entry.", "tokens": [50419, 1133, 291, 9773, 257, 5389, 281, 12362, 1045, 11, 264, 10336, 23815, 257, 5893, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 8729, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16447540231653163, "compression_ratio": 1.504950495049505, "no_speech_prob": 1.1737641024064938e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 73726, "start": 743.24, "end": 752.9, "text": " This takes a highly condensed piece of front matter, basically a description of what the skill does and when to use it, and permanently pins it into the resident system prompt.", "tokens": [50664, 639, 2516, 257, 5405, 36398, 2522, 295, 1868, 1871, 11, 1936, 257, 3855, 295, 437, 264, 5389, 775, 293, 562, 281, 764, 309, 11, 293, 24042, 16392, 309, 666, 264, 10832, 1185, 12391, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16447540231653163, "compression_ratio": 1.504950495049505, "no_speech_prob": 1.1737641024064938e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 73726, "start": 753.3199999999999, "end": 754.16, "text": " And what does that cost?", "tokens": [51168, 400, 437, 775, 300, 2063, 30, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16447540231653163, "compression_ratio": 1.504950495049505, "no_speech_prob": 1.1737641024064938e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 75416, "start": 754.16, "end": 758.12, "text": " It costs anywhere from 50 to 100 precious tokens per skill.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5497, 4992, 490, 2625, 281, 2319, 12406, 22667, 680, 5389, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 75416, "start": 758.3399999999999, "end": 765.66, "text": " So Yin's team empirically proved that simply reading a skill's content does not actually require that skill to be resident in the prompt.", "tokens": [50574, 407, 33254, 311, 1469, 25790, 984, 14617, 300, 2935, 3760, 257, 5389, 311, 2701, 775, 406, 767, 3651, 300, 5389, 281, 312, 10832, 294, 264, 12391, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 75416, "start": 765.98, "end": 770.52, "text": " They effectively decoupled the concept of availability from the concept of residency.", "tokens": [50956, 814, 8659, 979, 263, 15551, 264, 3410, 295, 17945, 490, 264, 3410, 295, 34014, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 75416, "start": 771.16, "end": 775.7199999999999, "text": " You only pay the 50 token prompt tax when you explicitly require the auto-triggering behavior.", "tokens": [51215, 509, 787, 1689, 264, 2625, 14862, 12391, 3366, 562, 291, 20803, 3651, 264, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 5223, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 75416, "start": 775.8, "end": 776.3199999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51447, 7587, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 75416, "start": 776.48, "end": 778.4399999999999, "text": " But this is exactly where the fliction paper steps in.", "tokens": [51481, 583, 341, 307, 2293, 689, 264, 932, 4105, 3035, 4439, 294, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 75416, "start": 778.78, "end": 781.5799999999999, "text": " And honestly, this is where I initially had some serious pushback.", "tokens": [51596, 400, 6095, 11, 341, 307, 689, 286, 9105, 632, 512, 3156, 2944, 3207, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 75416, "start": 781.64, "end": 782.0799999999999, "text": " Oh, really?", "tokens": [51739, 876, 11, 534, 30, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 75416, "start": 782.52, "end": 783.24, "text": " What was your hesitation?", "tokens": [51783, 708, 390, 428, 36125, 30, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1705478056696535, "compression_ratio": 1.6475903614457832, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355744461762686e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 78324, "start": 783.24, "end": 786.7, "text": " My hesitation was, okay, so they broke one button into three buttons.", "tokens": [50365, 1222, 36125, 390, 11, 1392, 11, 370, 436, 6902, 472, 2960, 666, 1045, 9905, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 78324, "start": 786.92, "end": 789.82, "text": " That sounds like basic practical software engineering.", "tokens": [50549, 663, 3263, 411, 3875, 8496, 4722, 7043, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 78324, "start": 790.04, "end": 796.42, "text": " Why do we need an intensely dense theoretical paper relying on 1980s type theory to explain this?", "tokens": [50705, 1545, 360, 321, 643, 364, 43235, 18011, 20864, 3035, 24140, 322, 13626, 82, 2010, 5261, 281, 2903, 341, 30, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 78324, "start": 797.14, "end": 802.4, "text": " Yin's team looked at the token constraints, realized the bundle was too heavy, and refactored the software.", "tokens": [51060, 33254, 311, 1469, 2956, 412, 264, 14862, 18491, 11, 5334, 264, 24438, 390, 886, 4676, 11, 293, 1895, 578, 2769, 264, 4722, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 78324, "start": 802.9, "end": 804.0, "text": " It's smart optimization.", "tokens": [51348, 467, 311, 4069, 19618, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 78324, "start": 804.76, "end": 809.7, "text": " Why is fliction dragging decades-old mathematics into a 2026 software update?", "tokens": [51441, 1545, 307, 932, 4105, 24385, 7878, 12, 2641, 18666, 666, 257, 945, 10880, 4722, 5623, 30, 51688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13823919296264647, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839899057858541e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 80970, "start": 809.7, "end": 819.7, "text": " It's a very fair question, because if Yin at all just found a clever workaround for current hardware limitations, then the at-skills protocol is just a temporary patch, right?", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 588, 3143, 1168, 11, 570, 498, 33254, 412, 439, 445, 1352, 257, 13494, 589, 25762, 337, 2190, 8837, 15705, 11, 550, 264, 412, 12, 5161, 2565, 10336, 307, 445, 257, 13413, 9972, 11, 558, 30, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 80970, "start": 819.72, "end": 819.9000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50866, 1779, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 80970, "start": 819.98, "end": 822.82, "text": " Like, we'll get bigger context windows eventually, and the patch won't matter.", "tokens": [50879, 1743, 11, 321, 603, 483, 3801, 4319, 9309, 4728, 11, 293, 264, 9972, 1582, 380, 1871, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 80970, "start": 822.84, "end": 823.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51022, 7587, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 80970, "start": 823.46, "end": 826.74, "text": " But fliction's core argument is that Yin didn't just find a neat trick.", "tokens": [51053, 583, 932, 4105, 311, 4965, 6770, 307, 300, 33254, 994, 380, 445, 915, 257, 10654, 4282, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 80970, "start": 827.1600000000001, "end": 830.32, "text": " Yin empirically stumbled blindly into a rigid mathematical boundary.", "tokens": [51238, 33254, 25790, 984, 36668, 47744, 666, 257, 22195, 18894, 12866, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13072115832036085, "compression_ratio": 1.5166051660516606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891274419474241e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 83032, "start": 830.32, "end": 838.6800000000001, "text": " Fliction is asserting that the distinction between a zero-cost bare reference and a 50-token installed line isn't a quirk of transformer architectures at all.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 307, 1256, 27187, 300, 264, 16844, 1296, 257, 4018, 12, 27718, 6949, 6408, 293, 257, 2625, 12, 83, 8406, 8899, 1622, 1943, 380, 257, 421, 18610, 295, 31782, 6331, 1303, 412, 439, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520731651176841, "compression_ratio": 1.3941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.4369363988617212e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 83032, "start": 838.7800000000001, "end": 839.4000000000001, "text": " Then what is it?", "tokens": [50788, 1396, 437, 307, 309, 30, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520731651176841, "compression_ratio": 1.3941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.4369363988617212e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 83032, "start": 839.5400000000001, "end": 842.7800000000001, "text": " It is the physical manifestation of relational parametricity.", "tokens": [50826, 467, 307, 264, 4001, 29550, 295, 38444, 6220, 17475, 507, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520731651176841, "compression_ratio": 1.3941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.4369363988617212e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 84278, "start": 842.78, "end": 850.88, "text": " Okay, here's where it gets really interesting, because this is where we transition from software engineering into pure type theory, and we aren't going to water this down.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 510, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 11, 570, 341, 307, 689, 321, 6034, 490, 4722, 7043, 666, 6075, 2010, 5261, 11, 293, 321, 3212, 380, 516, 281, 1281, 341, 760, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05022695038344834, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.775827098218774e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 84278, "start": 851.5799999999999, "end": 864.06, "text": " Fliction anchors this entire argument in John Reynolds' 1983 theory of relational parametricity, and specifically Philip Wadler's famous 1989 paper, Theorems for Free.", "tokens": [50805, 3235, 4105, 12723, 830, 341, 2302, 6770, 294, 2619, 29516, 6, 31758, 5261, 295, 38444, 6220, 17475, 507, 11, 293, 4682, 21144, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 4618, 22427, 3035, 11, 440, 418, 2592, 337, 11551, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05022695038344834, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.775827098218774e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 84278, "start": 864.3, "end": 867.5799999999999, "text": " Yes, Wadler's paper is legendary in functional programming.", "tokens": [51441, 1079, 11, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 3035, 307, 16698, 294, 11745, 9410, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05022695038344834, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.775827098218774e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 86758, "start": 867.58, "end": 872.9000000000001, "text": " So we need to unpack what a free theorem actually is in the context of polymorphic functions.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 321, 643, 281, 26699, 437, 257, 1737, 20904, 767, 307, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 6754, 76, 18191, 299, 6828, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10609196171616063, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 86758, "start": 873.0600000000001, "end": 873.5200000000001, "text": " Let's do it.", "tokens": [50639, 961, 311, 360, 309, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10609196171616063, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 86758, "start": 873.84, "end": 880.32, "text": " So in functional programming, a polymorphic function is one that is defined uniformly over a generic type variable.", "tokens": [50678, 407, 294, 11745, 9410, 11, 257, 6754, 76, 18191, 299, 2445, 307, 472, 300, 307, 7642, 48806, 670, 257, 19577, 2010, 7006, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10609196171616063, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 86758, "start": 880.6800000000001, "end": 889.38, "text": " It's designed to operate on a container, like a list, a tree, or a stream, without needing to know anything about the specific data types residing inside that container.", "tokens": [51020, 467, 311, 4761, 281, 9651, 322, 257, 10129, 11, 411, 257, 1329, 11, 257, 4230, 11, 420, 257, 4309, 11, 1553, 18006, 281, 458, 1340, 466, 264, 2685, 1412, 3467, 725, 2819, 1854, 300, 10129, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10609196171616063, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 86758, "start": 889.5200000000001, "end": 889.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51462, 1779, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10609196171616063, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 88970, "start": 889.7, "end": 898.1400000000001, "text": " So a list of integers, a list of strings, a list of complex objects, the polymorphic function interacts with the structure of the container, not the semantics of the elements.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 257, 1329, 295, 41674, 11, 257, 1329, 295, 13985, 11, 257, 1329, 295, 3997, 6565, 11, 264, 6754, 76, 18191, 299, 2445, 43582, 365, 264, 3877, 295, 264, 10129, 11, 406, 264, 4361, 45298, 295, 264, 4959, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09541828632354736, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368571215992888e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 88970, "start": 898.58, "end": 902.0200000000001, "text": " Okay, and Wadler asked a highly specific question about these functions.", "tokens": [50809, 1033, 11, 293, 343, 345, 1918, 2351, 257, 5405, 2685, 1168, 466, 613, 6828, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09541828632354736, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368571215992888e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 90202, "start": 902.02, "end": 912.38, "text": " If you apply an arbitrary transformation to the underlying data within the container, does the polymorphic function operating on that container still behave identically?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 3079, 364, 23211, 9887, 281, 264, 14217, 1412, 1951, 264, 10129, 11, 775, 264, 6754, 76, 18191, 299, 2445, 7447, 322, 300, 10129, 920, 15158, 2473, 984, 30, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09068937186735222, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269228160168623e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 90202, "start": 912.68, "end": 913.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50898, 7587, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09068937186735222, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269228160168623e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 90202, "start": 913.66, "end": 920.12, "text": " Does its internal logic transport across the transformation automatically, simply by virtue of its type signature?", "tokens": [50947, 4402, 1080, 6920, 9952, 5495, 2108, 264, 9887, 6772, 11, 2935, 538, 20816, 295, 1080, 2010, 13397, 30, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09068937186735222, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269228160168623e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 90202, "start": 920.52, "end": 927.26, "text": " Or do you have to establish an explicit binding rule, a hypothesis, to guarantee that the function won't break?", "tokens": [51290, 1610, 360, 291, 362, 281, 8327, 364, 13691, 17359, 4978, 11, 257, 17291, 11, 281, 10815, 300, 264, 2445, 1582, 380, 1821, 30, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09068937186735222, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269228160168623e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 92726, "start": 927.26, "end": 932.28, "text": " Right. And Wadler proved that these functions basically bifurcate into two fundamental categories.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 343, 345, 1918, 14617, 300, 613, 6828, 1936, 272, 351, 374, 66, 473, 666, 732, 8088, 10479, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08004236757085564, "compression_ratio": 1.766355140186916, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 92726, "start": 932.9399999999999, "end": 936.74, "text": " The first category consists of what he called genuinely parametric functions.", "tokens": [50649, 440, 700, 7719, 14689, 295, 437, 415, 1219, 17839, 6220, 17475, 6828, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08004236757085564, "compression_ratio": 1.766355140186916, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 92726, "start": 937.16, "end": 938.04, "text": " These are unconditional.", "tokens": [50860, 1981, 366, 47916, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08004236757085564, "compression_ratio": 1.766355140186916, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 92726, "start": 938.56, "end": 947.54, "text": " Functions like head, which extracts the first element of a list, or tail, which returns the list minus the first element, or frist, which projects the first element of a tuple.", "tokens": [50930, 11166, 3916, 411, 1378, 11, 597, 8947, 82, 264, 700, 4478, 295, 257, 1329, 11, 420, 6838, 11, 597, 11247, 264, 1329, 3175, 264, 700, 4478, 11, 420, 431, 468, 11, 597, 4455, 264, 700, 4478, 295, 257, 2604, 781, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08004236757085564, "compression_ratio": 1.766355140186916, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 94754, "start": 947.54, "end": 964.62, "text": " Right. So if I have a generic list a, and I apply an arbitrary function f to transform every element of a, Wadler's theorem dictates that extracting the head of the list first and then transforming that single extracted item yields the exact same result as transforming the entire list first and then extracting the head.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 407, 498, 286, 362, 257, 19577, 1329, 257, 11, 293, 286, 3079, 364, 23211, 2445, 283, 281, 4088, 633, 4478, 295, 257, 11, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 20904, 12569, 1024, 300, 49844, 264, 1378, 295, 264, 1329, 700, 293, 550, 27210, 300, 2167, 34086, 3174, 32168, 264, 1900, 912, 1874, 382, 27210, 264, 2302, 1329, 700, 293, 550, 49844, 264, 1378, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07695131178026075, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047266797995622e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 94754, "start": 964.76, "end": 966.4, "text": " The operation commutes flawlessly.", "tokens": [51226, 440, 6916, 800, 1819, 13717, 12048, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07695131178026075, "compression_ratio": 1.7623762376237624, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047266797995622e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 96640, "start": 966.4, "end": 968.3, "text": " Flawlessly and unconditionally.", "tokens": [50365, 479, 5901, 12048, 293, 34959, 15899, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16260981559753418, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983203259170575e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 96640, "start": 969.06, "end": 975.8199999999999, "text": " The head function doesn't care if the data changes from integers to strings, or if it moves from one memory register to another.", "tokens": [50498, 440, 1378, 2445, 1177, 380, 1127, 498, 264, 1412, 2962, 490, 41674, 281, 13985, 11, 420, 498, 309, 6067, 490, 472, 4675, 7280, 281, 1071, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16260981559753418, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983203259170575e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 96640, "start": 976.4599999999999, "end": 984.4599999999999, "text": " Because its specification is completely silent on the properties of the data, it demands no structural assumptions from that data.", "tokens": [50868, 1436, 1080, 31256, 307, 2584, 12784, 322, 264, 7221, 295, 264, 1412, 11, 309, 15107, 572, 15067, 17695, 490, 300, 1412, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16260981559753418, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983203259170575e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 96640, "start": 985.04, "end": 988.5799999999999, "text": " You get the preservation of its behavior entirely for free.", "tokens": [51297, 509, 483, 264, 27257, 295, 1080, 5223, 7696, 337, 1737, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16260981559753418, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983203259170575e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 98858, "start": 988.58, "end": 990.5, "text": " I always think of the head function like this.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 1009, 519, 295, 264, 1378, 2445, 411, 341, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 98858, "start": 991.1, "end": 1000.6800000000001, "text": " It's like saying, it doesn't matter if I pull the top card off a deck and then paint it blue, or if I paint the whole deck blue and then pull off the top card, the result is the identical blue card.", "tokens": [50491, 467, 311, 411, 1566, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1871, 498, 286, 2235, 264, 1192, 2920, 766, 257, 9341, 293, 550, 4225, 309, 3344, 11, 420, 498, 286, 4225, 264, 1379, 9341, 3344, 293, 550, 2235, 766, 264, 1192, 2920, 11, 264, 1874, 307, 264, 14800, 3344, 2920, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 98858, "start": 1000.76, "end": 1001.98, "text": " No special rules needed.", "tokens": [50974, 883, 2121, 4474, 2978, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 98858, "start": 1002.2800000000001, "end": 1003.2800000000001, "text": " That's exactly right.", "tokens": [51050, 663, 311, 2293, 558, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 98858, "start": 1003.5, "end": 1007.5, "text": " But then Wadler identifies the second category, conditional functions.", "tokens": [51111, 583, 550, 343, 345, 1918, 34597, 264, 1150, 7719, 11, 27708, 6828, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 98858, "start": 1007.76, "end": 1011.2800000000001, "text": " And this includes operations like sort, filter, and fold.", "tokens": [51324, 400, 341, 5974, 7705, 411, 1333, 11, 6608, 11, 293, 4860, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 98858, "start": 1011.44, "end": 1012.32, "text": " Right. Heavy hitters.", "tokens": [51508, 1779, 13, 26473, 2045, 1559, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11145503002664317, "compression_ratio": 1.6973180076628354, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171632175737694e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 101232, "start": 1012.32, "end": 1019.88, "text": " Yeah. And these functions cannot be genuinely parametric because they are forced to consume additional structure to execute their logic.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 400, 613, 6828, 2644, 312, 17839, 6220, 17475, 570, 436, 366, 7579, 281, 14732, 4497, 3877, 281, 14483, 641, 9952, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 101232, "start": 1020.1400000000001, "end": 1022.7600000000001, "text": " Okay, let's break down the sort example because this is crucial.", "tokens": [50756, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 1333, 1365, 570, 341, 307, 11462, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 101232, "start": 1023.0600000000001, "end": 1024.5, "text": " Right. So look closely at sort.", "tokens": [50902, 1779, 13, 407, 574, 8185, 412, 1333, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 101232, "start": 1024.9, "end": 1028.24, "text": " You cannot sort a generic container without an ordering relation.", "tokens": [50994, 509, 2644, 1333, 257, 19577, 10129, 1553, 364, 21739, 9721, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 101232, "start": 1029.04, "end": 1035.0, "text": " The function fundamentally relies on the ability to compare element X to element Y and determine precedence.", "tokens": [51201, 440, 2445, 17879, 30910, 322, 264, 3485, 281, 6794, 4478, 1783, 281, 4478, 398, 293, 6997, 16969, 655, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 101232, "start": 1035.6200000000001, "end": 1041.24, "text": " Therefore, if you apply an arbitrary transformation F to your data, does sort commute?", "tokens": [51530, 7504, 11, 498, 291, 3079, 364, 23211, 9887, 479, 281, 428, 1412, 11, 775, 1333, 36750, 30, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14448972917952627, "compression_ratio": 1.6555183946488294, "no_speech_prob": 1.37784466995583e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 104124, "start": 1041.24, "end": 1042.94, "text": " No, absolutely not.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 3122, 406, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 104124, "start": 1043.06, "end": 1053.38, "text": " Like, if I have an ordered list of integers and my transformation F is a cryptographic hash function, the resulting hashes will not preserve the numerical order of the original integers.", "tokens": [50456, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 362, 364, 8866, 1329, 295, 41674, 293, 452, 9887, 479, 307, 257, 9844, 12295, 22019, 2445, 11, 264, 16505, 575, 8076, 486, 406, 15665, 264, 29054, 1668, 295, 264, 3380, 41674, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 104124, "start": 1054.06, "end": 1059.54, "text": " The data is scrambled, and the sort operation's output is corrupted because the assumed structure was destroyed.", "tokens": [51006, 440, 1412, 307, 49127, 11, 293, 264, 1333, 6916, 311, 5598, 307, 39480, 570, 264, 15895, 3877, 390, 8937, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 104124, "start": 1059.78, "end": 1060.38, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51292, 48746, 736, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 104124, "start": 1061.0, "end": 1063.9, "text": " Therefore, sort does not yield a theorem for free.", "tokens": [51353, 7504, 11, 1333, 775, 406, 11257, 257, 20904, 337, 1737, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 104124, "start": 1064.44, "end": 1067.78, "text": " Commutation for sort requires an explicit binding hypothesis.", "tokens": [51525, 3046, 11380, 337, 1333, 7029, 364, 13691, 17359, 17291, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14390540845466382, "compression_ratio": 1.5992779783393503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312378101595137e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 106778, "start": 1067.78, "end": 1073.2, "text": " You can only apply a transformation if that transformation strictly preserves the ordering relation.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 787, 3079, 257, 9887, 498, 300, 9887, 20792, 1183, 9054, 264, 21739, 9721, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113508158716663, "compression_ratio": 1.5375722543352601, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040636259181175e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 106778, "start": 1073.36, "end": 1074.52, "text": " The structure must be protected.", "tokens": [50644, 440, 3877, 1633, 312, 10594, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113508158716663, "compression_ratio": 1.5375722543352601, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040636259181175e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 106778, "start": 1074.7, "end": 1080.56, "text": " Exactly. You are mathematically obligated to purchase that protection if you want the function to survive the change.", "tokens": [50711, 7587, 13, 509, 366, 44003, 9270, 770, 281, 8110, 300, 6334, 498, 291, 528, 264, 2445, 281, 7867, 264, 1319, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113508158716663, "compression_ratio": 1.5375722543352601, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040636259181175e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 106778, "start": 1080.8, "end": 1081.44, "text": " Wait, hold on.", "tokens": [51016, 3802, 11, 1797, 322, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113508158716663, "compression_ratio": 1.5375722543352601, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040636259181175e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 108144, "start": 1081.44, "end": 1092.1200000000001, "text": " If that token cost in the at-skills protocol is actually the physical artifact of this structural obligation, then prompt engineering isn't just about hacking the system with clever keywords.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 300, 14862, 2063, 294, 264, 412, 12, 5161, 2565, 10336, 307, 767, 264, 4001, 34806, 295, 341, 15067, 20326, 11, 550, 12391, 7043, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 31422, 264, 1185, 365, 13494, 21009, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16370272232314287, "compression_ratio": 1.5154639175257731, "no_speech_prob": 1.769170530560582e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 108144, "start": 1092.3600000000001, "end": 1094.66, "text": " It is literally applied type theory.", "tokens": [50911, 467, 307, 3736, 6456, 2010, 5261, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16370272232314287, "compression_ratio": 1.5154639175257731, "no_speech_prob": 1.769170530560582e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 108144, "start": 1094.8600000000001, "end": 1098.78, "text": " We are negotiating mathematical boundaries using token economics.", "tokens": [51036, 492, 366, 30396, 18894, 13180, 1228, 14862, 14564, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16370272232314287, "compression_ratio": 1.5154639175257731, "no_speech_prob": 1.769170530560582e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 109878, "start": 1098.78, "end": 1106.86, "text": " Yes. This is the exact mapping that Flixion performs to bridge the 1989 math with the 2026 AI architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 639, 307, 264, 1900, 18350, 300, 3235, 970, 313, 26213, 281, 7283, 264, 22427, 5221, 365, 264, 945, 10880, 7318, 9482, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13515107696120804, "compression_ratio": 1.3919597989949748, "no_speech_prob": 1.882576776759959e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 109878, "start": 1107.6399999999999, "end": 1116.1, "text": " Flixion says, let's look at the three tiers of Yin's protocol resolve, save, and trigger, and map them directly onto Wadler's functional categories.", "tokens": [50808, 3235, 970, 313, 1619, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 1045, 40563, 295, 33254, 311, 10336, 14151, 11, 3155, 11, 293, 7875, 11, 293, 4471, 552, 3838, 3911, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 11745, 10479, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13515107696120804, "compression_ratio": 1.3919597989949748, "no_speech_prob": 1.882576776759959e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 109878, "start": 1116.22, "end": 1116.8999999999999, "text": " Okay, let's do that.", "tokens": [51237, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 360, 300, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13515107696120804, "compression_ratio": 1.3919597989949748, "no_speech_prob": 1.882576776759959e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 111690, "start": 1116.9, "end": 1121.8000000000002, "text": " In this mapping, the transformation we are applying isn't changing an integer to a string.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 18350, 11, 264, 9887, 321, 366, 9275, 1943, 380, 4473, 364, 24922, 281, 257, 6798, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 111690, "start": 1121.98, "end": 1123.0800000000002, "text": " It's a change in representation.", "tokens": [50619, 467, 311, 257, 1319, 294, 10290, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 111690, "start": 1123.68, "end": 1128.3000000000002, "text": " It is the act of moving a skill from a remote server to a local disk to an active memory cache.", "tokens": [50704, 467, 307, 264, 605, 295, 2684, 257, 5389, 490, 257, 8607, 7154, 281, 257, 2654, 12355, 281, 364, 4967, 4675, 19459, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 111690, "start": 1128.52, "end": 1131.7800000000002, "text": " We are changing where and how the data physically lives.", "tokens": [50946, 492, 366, 4473, 689, 293, 577, 264, 1412, 9762, 2909, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 111690, "start": 1131.9, "end": 1133.24, "text": " Let's trace that execution path.", "tokens": [51115, 961, 311, 13508, 300, 15058, 3100, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 111690, "start": 1133.3200000000002, "end": 1135.0, "text": " We start with Tier 1, the bare reference.", "tokens": [51186, 492, 722, 365, 24224, 502, 11, 264, 6949, 6408, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 111690, "start": 1135.6000000000001, "end": 1140.14, "text": " Flixion categorizes the act of reading a skill via path as the resolve operation.", "tokens": [51300, 3235, 970, 313, 19250, 5660, 264, 605, 295, 3760, 257, 5389, 5766, 3100, 382, 264, 14151, 6916, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 111690, "start": 1140.68, "end": 1143.0600000000002, "text": " And Flixion now maps resolve directly to the head function.", "tokens": [51554, 400, 3235, 970, 313, 586, 11317, 14151, 3838, 281, 264, 1378, 2445, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12947308632635302, "compression_ratio": 1.7177700348432057, "no_speech_prob": 2.408333515252492e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 114306, "start": 1143.06, "end": 1148.04, "text": " And it maps perfectly because the specification of resolve is entirely silent on representation.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 11317, 6239, 570, 264, 31256, 295, 14151, 307, 7696, 12784, 322, 10290, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11816134398010955, "compression_ratio": 1.6509803921568627, "no_speech_prob": 2.871549786148675e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 114306, "start": 1148.44, "end": 1154.46, "text": " The orchestration layer merely asks, does this specific path point to this specific sequence of bytes?", "tokens": [50634, 440, 14161, 2405, 4583, 17003, 8962, 11, 775, 341, 2685, 3100, 935, 281, 341, 2685, 8310, 295, 36088, 30, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11816134398010955, "compression_ratio": 1.6509803921568627, "no_speech_prob": 2.871549786148675e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 114306, "start": 1154.96, "end": 1161.84, "text": " As long as the semantic identity of the content remains intact, you can radically transform the storage representation.", "tokens": [50960, 1018, 938, 382, 264, 47982, 6575, 295, 264, 2701, 7023, 23493, 11, 291, 393, 35508, 4088, 264, 6725, 10290, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11816134398010955, "compression_ratio": 1.6509803921568627, "no_speech_prob": 2.871549786148675e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 114306, "start": 1162.5, "end": 1168.58, "text": " You can shift the skill from a GitHub repo to an ephemeral Docker volume to a local hard drive cache.", "tokens": [51337, 509, 393, 5513, 264, 5389, 490, 257, 23331, 49040, 281, 364, 308, 41245, 2790, 33772, 5523, 281, 257, 2654, 1152, 3332, 19459, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11816134398010955, "compression_ratio": 1.6509803921568627, "no_speech_prob": 2.871549786148675e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 116858, "start": 1168.58, "end": 1173.9199999999998, "text": " The resolve operation will still cleanly fetch the markdown into the execution context.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 14151, 6916, 486, 920, 2541, 356, 23673, 264, 1491, 5093, 666, 264, 15058, 4319, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 116858, "start": 1174.4399999999998, "end": 1177.48, "text": " So it commutes across the representation change unconditionally.", "tokens": [50658, 407, 309, 800, 1819, 2108, 264, 10290, 1319, 34959, 15899, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 116858, "start": 1177.5, "end": 1178.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50811, 7587, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 116858, "start": 1178.3999999999999, "end": 1179.6799999999998, "text": " It demands no extra structure.", "tokens": [50856, 467, 15107, 572, 2857, 3877, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 116858, "start": 1179.8999999999999, "end": 1181.3, "text": " It is a theorem for free.", "tokens": [50931, 467, 307, 257, 20904, 337, 1737, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 116858, "start": 1181.6799999999998, "end": 1185.56, "text": " This brings us to Tier 2, the saved copy or the saved ebriation.", "tokens": [51020, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 24224, 568, 11, 264, 6624, 5055, 420, 264, 6624, 308, 65, 470, 399, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 116858, "start": 1185.8999999999999, "end": 1188.6, "text": " Flixion maps this to Flixion's tuple projection function.", "tokens": [51231, 3235, 970, 313, 11317, 341, 281, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 2604, 781, 22743, 2445, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 116858, "start": 1189.46, "end": 1193.52, "text": " Let's dig into the memory pointer mechanics of this because this is where the architecture really shines.", "tokens": [51409, 961, 311, 2528, 666, 264, 4675, 23918, 12939, 295, 341, 570, 341, 307, 689, 264, 9482, 534, 28056, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 116858, "start": 1193.6399999999999, "end": 1194.26, "text": " It's very clever.", "tokens": [51618, 467, 311, 588, 13494, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17853882733513327, "compression_ratio": 1.648936170212766, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206809687737e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 119426, "start": 1194.26, "end": 1199.42, "text": " When you save a skill locally in the AdSkills protocol, you aren't just downloading raw text.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 3155, 257, 5389, 16143, 294, 264, 1999, 50, 74, 2565, 10336, 11, 291, 3212, 380, 445, 32529, 8936, 2487, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433381615104256, "compression_ratio": 1.5739130434782609, "no_speech_prob": 3.1656179413919183e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 119426, "start": 1199.7, "end": 1205.52, "text": " You are actually generating a tuple composed of two elements, the content itself and a provenance stamp.", "tokens": [50637, 509, 366, 767, 17746, 257, 2604, 781, 18204, 295, 732, 4959, 11, 264, 2701, 2564, 293, 257, 12785, 719, 9921, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433381615104256, "compression_ratio": 1.5739130434782609, "no_speech_prob": 3.1656179413919183e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 119426, "start": 1205.74, "end": 1208.14, "text": " The provenance stamp is vital metadata.", "tokens": [50939, 440, 12785, 719, 9921, 307, 11707, 26603, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433381615104256, "compression_ratio": 1.5739130434782609, "no_speech_prob": 3.1656179413919183e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 119426, "start": 1208.82, "end": 1214.56, "text": " It records the exact origin URI, the commit hash, the timestamp, and the localized dependency graph.", "tokens": [51093, 467, 7724, 264, 1900, 4957, 624, 5577, 11, 264, 5599, 22019, 11, 264, 49108, 1215, 11, 293, 264, 44574, 33621, 4295, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433381615104256, "compression_ratio": 1.5739130434782609, "no_speech_prob": 3.1656179413919183e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 119426, "start": 1214.8799999999999, "end": 1216.04, "text": " It is the audit trail.", "tokens": [51396, 467, 307, 264, 17748, 9924, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433381615104256, "compression_ratio": 1.5739130434782609, "no_speech_prob": 3.1656179413919183e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 121604, "start": 1216.04, "end": 1224.7, "text": " But when the agent's runtime environment calls the resolve function on that locally saved skill, the architecture deliberately executes a projection.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 264, 9461, 311, 34474, 2823, 5498, 264, 14151, 2445, 322, 300, 16143, 6624, 5389, 11, 264, 9482, 23506, 4454, 1819, 257, 22743, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0975190652044196, "compression_ratio": 1.5876777251184835, "no_speech_prob": 2.417733764928376e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 121604, "start": 1225.48, "end": 1233.68, "text": " It takes the tuple of content and provenance, isolates the content, and injects only the content into the LLM's context window.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 2516, 264, 2604, 781, 295, 2701, 293, 12785, 719, 11, 7381, 1024, 264, 2701, 11, 293, 10711, 82, 787, 264, 2701, 666, 264, 441, 43, 44, 311, 4319, 4910, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0975190652044196, "compression_ratio": 1.5876777251184835, "no_speech_prob": 2.417733764928376e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 121604, "start": 1234.22, "end": 1237.26, "text": " The provenance stamp is left entirely behind on the disk.", "tokens": [51274, 440, 12785, 719, 9921, 307, 1411, 7696, 2261, 322, 264, 12355, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0975190652044196, "compression_ratio": 1.5876777251184835, "no_speech_prob": 2.417733764928376e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 123726, "start": 1237.26, "end": 1240.68, "text": " It aggressively drops the second half of the tuple, exactly like Flixion.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 32024, 11438, 264, 1150, 1922, 295, 264, 2604, 781, 11, 2293, 411, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 123726, "start": 1240.76, "end": 1243.18, "text": " And by doing so, it creates a non-interference guarantee.", "tokens": [50540, 400, 538, 884, 370, 11, 309, 7829, 257, 2107, 12, 5106, 5158, 10815, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 123726, "start": 1243.74, "end": 1245.0, "text": " You can update the provenance stamp.", "tokens": [50689, 509, 393, 5623, 264, 12785, 719, 9921, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 123726, "start": 1245.08, "end": 1246.62, "text": " You can change the local file path.", "tokens": [50756, 509, 393, 1319, 264, 2654, 3991, 3100, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 123726, "start": 1246.9, "end": 1248.26, "text": " You can alter the git commit history.", "tokens": [50847, 509, 393, 11337, 264, 18331, 5599, 2503, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 123726, "start": 1248.72, "end": 1252.2, "text": " You can apply vast representational transformations to the metadata.", "tokens": [50938, 509, 393, 3079, 8369, 2906, 1478, 34852, 281, 264, 26603, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 123726, "start": 1252.76, "end": 1259.26, "text": " But because the runtime structurally ignores everything but the content during injection, the execution remains perfectly invariant.", "tokens": [51140, 583, 570, 264, 34474, 6594, 6512, 5335, 2706, 1203, 457, 264, 2701, 1830, 22873, 11, 264, 15058, 7023, 6239, 33270, 394, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 123726, "start": 1259.36, "end": 1260.18, "text": " Another free theorem.", "tokens": [51470, 3996, 1737, 20904, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 123726, "start": 1260.66, "end": 1262.08, "text": " Zero standing token cost.", "tokens": [51535, 17182, 4877, 14862, 2063, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 123726, "start": 1262.22, "end": 1263.36, "text": " But then we hit tier 3.", "tokens": [51613, 583, 550, 321, 2045, 12362, 805, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 123726, "start": 1263.82, "end": 1264.56, "text": " Auto-triggering.", "tokens": [51693, 13738, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 123726, "start": 1264.86, "end": 1265.7, "text": " The trigger operation.", "tokens": [51745, 440, 7875, 6916, 13, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1912039075578962, "compression_ratio": 1.6746987951807228, "no_speech_prob": 1.85406225962359e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 126570, "start": 1265.7, "end": 1267.5800000000002, "text": " Flixion maps this directly to sort.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 970, 313, 11317, 341, 3838, 281, 1333, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 126570, "start": 1267.96, "end": 1269.32, "text": " And this is where the free theorems end.", "tokens": [50478, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 1737, 10299, 2592, 917, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 126570, "start": 1269.52, "end": 1270.42, "text": " Completely end.", "tokens": [50556, 39978, 917, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 126570, "start": 1270.94, "end": 1273.1200000000001, "text": " Because trigger consumes additional structure.", "tokens": [50627, 1436, 7875, 48823, 4497, 3877, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 126570, "start": 1273.76, "end": 1284.18, "text": " To allow an agent to passively monitor a user's prompt and spontaneously decide to invoke a tool, the agent must have continuous resident awareness of that tool's capabilities.", "tokens": [50768, 1407, 2089, 364, 9461, 281, 1320, 3413, 6002, 257, 4195, 311, 12391, 293, 47632, 4536, 281, 41117, 257, 2290, 11, 264, 9461, 1633, 362, 10957, 10832, 8888, 295, 300, 2290, 311, 10862, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 126570, "start": 1284.44, "end": 1284.6200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51302, 1779, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 126570, "start": 1284.66, "end": 1286.6200000000001, "text": " It can't trigger what it doesn't know exists.", "tokens": [51313, 467, 393, 380, 7875, 437, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 8198, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 126570, "start": 1286.72, "end": 1287.1000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51416, 7587, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 126570, "start": 1287.92, "end": 1291.04, "text": " The operation is not defined over bare, floating data.", "tokens": [51476, 440, 6916, 307, 406, 7642, 670, 6949, 11, 12607, 1412, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 126570, "start": 1291.54, "end": 1294.28, "text": " It is fundamentally defined over a resident prompt.", "tokens": [51657, 467, 307, 17879, 7642, 670, 257, 10832, 12391, 13, 51794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15585286738508838, "compression_ratio": 1.6385135135135136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762456002573535e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 129428, "start": 1294.28, "end": 1298.36, "text": " Residency is the ordering relation of the LLM architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 5015, 23343, 307, 264, 21739, 9721, 295, 264, 441, 43, 44, 9482, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2265024325426887, "compression_ratio": 0.921875, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272151129267616e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 129836, "start": 1298.36, "end": 1310.82, "text": " If you apply a representational transformation that removes the skill's front matter from the acts of context window, say, migrating the skill back to a purely local disk file does trigger commute.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 3079, 257, 2906, 1478, 9887, 300, 30445, 264, 5389, 311, 1868, 1871, 490, 264, 10672, 295, 4319, 4910, 11, 584, 11, 6186, 8754, 264, 5389, 646, 281, 257, 17491, 2654, 12355, 3991, 775, 7875, 36750, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516824331039038, "compression_ratio": 1.5596330275229358, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619838101236684e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 129836, "start": 1311.24, "end": 1312.36, "text": " It breaks instantly.", "tokens": [51009, 467, 9857, 13518, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516824331039038, "compression_ratio": 1.5596330275229358, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619838101236684e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 129836, "start": 1313.06, "end": 1315.1599999999999, "text": " The agent becomes completely blind to the skill.", "tokens": [51100, 440, 9461, 3643, 2584, 6865, 281, 264, 5389, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516824331039038, "compression_ratio": 1.5596330275229358, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619838101236684e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 129836, "start": 1315.26, "end": 1318.3799999999999, "text": " It will never auto-trigger a tool it cannot see in its attention matrix.", "tokens": [51210, 467, 486, 1128, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 257, 2290, 309, 2644, 536, 294, 1080, 3202, 8141, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516824331039038, "compression_ratio": 1.5596330275229358, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619838101236684e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 131838, "start": 1318.38, "end": 1318.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 131838, "start": 1319.2800000000002, "end": 1322.66, "text": " Therefore, the trigger operation carries a strict, inescapable hypothesis.", "tokens": [50410, 7504, 11, 264, 7875, 6916, 16402, 257, 10910, 11, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 17291, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 131838, "start": 1323.5, "end": 1327.0800000000002, "text": " Any change in the system must preserve the prompt residency of the skill.", "tokens": [50621, 2639, 1319, 294, 264, 1185, 1633, 15665, 264, 12391, 34014, 295, 264, 5389, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 131838, "start": 1327.5400000000002, "end": 1329.3600000000001, "text": " And this is Flixion's breakthrough insight.", "tokens": [50823, 400, 341, 307, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 22397, 11269, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 131838, "start": 1329.5600000000002, "end": 1330.7, "text": " This part blew my mind.", "tokens": [50924, 639, 644, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 131838, "start": 1331.0400000000002, "end": 1334.74, "text": " That 50 to 100 token cost for the auto-trigger front matter.", "tokens": [50998, 663, 2625, 281, 2319, 14862, 2063, 337, 264, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 1868, 1871, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 131838, "start": 1335.46, "end": 1337.8200000000002, "text": " That isn't sloppy coding by Yin's team.", "tokens": [51219, 663, 1943, 380, 43684, 17720, 538, 33254, 311, 1469, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 131838, "start": 1338.18, "end": 1339.6000000000001, "text": " It isn't an arbitrary tax.", "tokens": [51355, 467, 1943, 380, 364, 23211, 3366, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17991282276271545, "compression_ratio": 1.4831932773109244, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232387612877264e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 133960, "start": 1339.6, "end": 1347.9599999999998, "text": " It is the physical computational materialization of the explicit hypothesis that the sort function mathematically requires.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 4001, 28270, 2527, 2144, 295, 264, 13691, 17291, 300, 264, 1333, 2445, 44003, 7029, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 133960, "start": 1348.36, "end": 1353.36, "text": " We are literally spending inference tokens to purchase their residency preservation hypothesis.", "tokens": [50803, 492, 366, 3736, 6434, 38253, 22667, 281, 8110, 641, 34014, 27257, 17291, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 133960, "start": 1353.3799999999999, "end": 1353.6999999999998, "text": " Oh, yes.", "tokens": [51054, 876, 11, 2086, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 133960, "start": 1354.08, "end": 1361.62, "text": " If you want the conditional feature of auto-triggering, you are mathematically forced to pay for the structural assumption that makes it possible.", "tokens": [51089, 759, 291, 528, 264, 27708, 4111, 295, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 11, 291, 366, 44003, 7579, 281, 1689, 337, 264, 15067, 15302, 300, 1669, 309, 1944, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 133960, "start": 1362.1599999999999, "end": 1364.5, "text": " Yin et al. didn't invent this boundary.", "tokens": [51493, 33254, 1030, 419, 13, 994, 380, 7962, 341, 12866, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 133960, "start": 1364.8799999999999, "end": 1367.32, "text": " They just built an interface that finally respected it.", "tokens": [51629, 814, 445, 3094, 364, 9226, 300, 2721, 20020, 309, 13, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13911021124456346, "compression_ratio": 1.6468531468531469, "no_speech_prob": 2.108363180222672e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 136732, "start": 1367.32, "end": 1372.9199999999998, "text": " They isolated the operations that yielded free theorems from the operations that demanded heavy structural commitments.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 14621, 264, 7705, 300, 11257, 292, 1737, 10299, 2592, 490, 264, 7705, 300, 28276, 4676, 15067, 26230, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 136732, "start": 1373.6399999999999, "end": 1379.6, "text": " But Flixion pushes this further, because once you understand the strict residency requirements of trigger, you have to ask,", "tokens": [50681, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 21020, 341, 3052, 11, 570, 1564, 291, 1223, 264, 10910, 34014, 7728, 295, 7875, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1029, 11, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 136732, "start": 1380.06, "end": 1384.3999999999999, "text": " how do these requirements scale when we attempt to execute complex, multi-step workflows?", "tokens": [51002, 577, 360, 613, 7728, 4373, 562, 321, 5217, 281, 14483, 3997, 11, 4825, 12, 16792, 43461, 30, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 136732, "start": 1384.76, "end": 1385.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51237, 1779, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 136732, "start": 1385.4399999999998, "end": 1389.08, "text": " Let's say I'm building an autonomous agent to handle a complex code refactor.", "tokens": [51271, 961, 311, 584, 286, 478, 2390, 364, 23797, 9461, 281, 4813, 257, 3997, 3089, 1895, 15104, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 136732, "start": 1389.4399999999998, "end": 1393.4399999999998, "text": " I needed to use a repository search skill to find the relevant files,", "tokens": [51471, 286, 2978, 281, 764, 257, 25841, 3164, 5389, 281, 915, 264, 7340, 7098, 11, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 136732, "start": 1393.6599999999999, "end": 1396.32, "text": " a static analysis skill to identify the bugs,", "tokens": [51682, 257, 13437, 5215, 5389, 281, 5876, 264, 15120, 11, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14704419798770194, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.748555185192291e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 139632, "start": 1396.32, "end": 1398.82, "text": " and a get-commit skill to push the fixes.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 257, 483, 12, 1112, 3508, 5389, 281, 2944, 264, 32539, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 139632, "start": 1399.6599999999999, "end": 1403.3, "text": " In the traditional install paradigm, where everything relies on auto-triggering,", "tokens": [50532, 682, 264, 5164, 3625, 24709, 11, 689, 1203, 30910, 322, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 11, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 139632, "start": 1403.6599999999999, "end": 1406.6799999999998, "text": " I have to rely on what Yin calls the trigger lottery.", "tokens": [50732, 286, 362, 281, 10687, 322, 437, 33254, 5498, 264, 7875, 27391, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 139632, "start": 1407.1599999999999, "end": 1411.76, "text": " The trigger lottery is the direct result of probabilistic matching in a resident prompt.", "tokens": [50907, 440, 7875, 27391, 307, 264, 2047, 1874, 295, 31959, 3142, 14324, 294, 257, 10832, 12391, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 139632, "start": 1412.1599999999999, "end": 1415.2, "text": " If you dump all three of those skills into the active context window,", "tokens": [51157, 759, 291, 11430, 439, 1045, 295, 729, 3942, 666, 264, 4967, 4319, 4910, 11, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 139632, "start": 1415.76, "end": 1421.8999999999999, "text": " the LLM has to independently evaluate the semantic relevance of each skill's front matter against your prompt.", "tokens": [51337, 264, 441, 43, 44, 575, 281, 21761, 13059, 264, 47982, 32684, 295, 1184, 5389, 311, 1868, 1871, 1970, 428, 12391, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 139632, "start": 1422.06, "end": 1422.72, "text": " It has to guess.", "tokens": [51652, 467, 575, 281, 2041, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16552058288029262, "compression_ratio": 1.6836363636363636, "no_speech_prob": 1.913088394298046e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 142272, "start": 1422.72, "end": 1426.26, "text": " Right. It has to probabilistically guess, ah, I need the serve skill,", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 467, 575, 281, 31959, 20458, 2041, 11, 3716, 11, 286, 643, 264, 4596, 5389, 11, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10190202732278843, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 142272, "start": 1426.38, "end": 1430.02, "text": " and then independently it has to guess, I also need the static analysis skill.", "tokens": [50548, 293, 550, 21761, 309, 575, 281, 2041, 11, 286, 611, 643, 264, 13437, 5215, 5389, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10190202732278843, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 142272, "start": 1430.26, "end": 1434.94, "text": " And since it's an LLM, every independent evaluation is subject to stochastic variation.", "tokens": [50742, 400, 1670, 309, 311, 364, 441, 43, 44, 11, 633, 6695, 13344, 307, 3983, 281, 342, 8997, 2750, 12990, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10190202732278843, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 142272, "start": 1435.64, "end": 1438.94, "text": " If you have a 90% chance of successfully auto-triggering each skill,", "tokens": [51011, 759, 291, 362, 257, 4289, 4, 2931, 295, 10727, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 1184, 5389, 11, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10190202732278843, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 142272, "start": 1439.44, "end": 1444.06, "text": " your chance of flawlessly triggering all three in the correct sequence drops to about 72%.", "tokens": [51201, 428, 2931, 295, 13717, 12048, 40406, 439, 1045, 294, 264, 3006, 8310, 11438, 281, 466, 18731, 6856, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10190202732278843, "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 144406, "start": 1444.06, "end": 1447.26, "text": " If you need five skills, you're essentially flipping coins.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 643, 1732, 3942, 11, 291, 434, 4476, 26886, 13561, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16719333056745858, "compression_ratio": 1.2272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.1974505548527645e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 144406, "start": 1447.72, "end": 1451.8799999999999, "text": " The architecture guarantees a decay in reliability as complexity increases.", "tokens": [50548, 440, 9482, 32567, 257, 21039, 294, 24550, 382, 14024, 8637, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16719333056745858, "compression_ratio": 1.2272727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 2.1974505548527645e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 145188, "start": 1451.88, "end": 1456.5, "text": " Which brings Fliction to the next theorem in Wadler's catalog, the fold operation.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5607, 3235, 4105, 281, 264, 958, 20904, 294, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 19746, 11, 264, 4860, 6916, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16314016217770783, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779820162874602e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 145188, "start": 1457.46, "end": 1463.3200000000002, "text": " Fold is a polymorphic function that processes a data structure and recombines its elements to build a return value.", "tokens": [50644, 24609, 307, 257, 6754, 76, 18191, 299, 2445, 300, 7555, 257, 1412, 3877, 293, 850, 3548, 1652, 1080, 4959, 281, 1322, 257, 2736, 2158, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16314016217770783, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779820162874602e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 145188, "start": 1463.98, "end": 1469.0200000000002, "text": " But Wadler proved that fold requires an exceptionally strong hypothesis to survive transformation.", "tokens": [50970, 583, 343, 345, 1918, 14617, 300, 4860, 7029, 364, 37807, 2068, 17291, 281, 7867, 9887, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16314016217770783, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779820162874602e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 145188, "start": 1469.68, "end": 1472.1200000000001, "text": " It requires an algebra homomorphism condition.", "tokens": [51255, 467, 7029, 364, 21989, 3655, 32702, 1434, 4188, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16314016217770783, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779820162874602e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 145188, "start": 1472.5400000000002, "end": 1476.3400000000001, "text": " The transformation must strictly preserve the specific combining operation itself.", "tokens": [51398, 440, 9887, 1633, 20792, 15665, 264, 2685, 21928, 6916, 2564, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16314016217770783, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779820162874602e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 147634, "start": 1476.34, "end": 1481.3799999999999, "text": " How does that mathematical condition map to executing our multi-step code refactor?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 300, 18894, 4188, 4471, 281, 32368, 527, 4825, 12, 16792, 3089, 1895, 15104, 30, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 147634, "start": 1481.72, "end": 1486.12, "text": " In the atSkills protocol, you bypass the trigger lottery by leaning heavily on Tier 1.", "tokens": [50634, 682, 264, 412, 50, 74, 2565, 10336, 11, 291, 24996, 264, 7875, 27391, 538, 23390, 10950, 322, 24224, 502, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 147634, "start": 1486.48, "end": 1488.8999999999999, "text": " You explicitly name the paths in your prompt.", "tokens": [50872, 509, 20803, 1315, 264, 14518, 294, 428, 12391, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 147634, "start": 1489.28, "end": 1489.6599999999999, "text": " You write,", "tokens": [51012, 509, 2464, 11, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 147634, "start": 1490.1, "end": 1491.72, "text": " Execute at githuburbupo search,", "tokens": [51053, 17662, 1169, 412, 290, 355, 836, 16659, 1010, 78, 3164, 11, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 147634, "start": 1492.06, "end": 1494.12, "text": " pass the output to at local static analysis,", "tokens": [51151, 1320, 264, 5598, 281, 412, 2654, 13437, 5215, 11, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 147634, "start": 1494.6, "end": 1496.6, "text": " and finalize with at githubit commit.", "tokens": [51278, 293, 2572, 1125, 365, 412, 290, 355, 836, 270, 5599, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 147634, "start": 1497.28, "end": 1502.1599999999999, "text": " By hardcoding the paths, you explicitly supply the combining algebra that fold demands.", "tokens": [51412, 3146, 1152, 66, 8616, 264, 14518, 11, 291, 20803, 5847, 264, 21928, 21989, 300, 4860, 15107, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 147634, "start": 1502.36, "end": 1505.74, "text": " You completely remove the stochastic evaluation from the routing layer.", "tokens": [51666, 509, 2584, 4159, 264, 342, 8997, 2750, 13344, 490, 264, 32722, 4583, 13, 51835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18731168998304262, "compression_ratio": 1.6459016393442623, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430422982386064e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 150574, "start": 1505.74, "end": 1508.52, "text": " The LLM doesn't have to guess which tools to use.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 441, 43, 44, 1177, 380, 362, 281, 2041, 597, 3873, 281, 764, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 150574, "start": 1508.74, "end": 1511.92, "text": " The execution graph is deterministically settled by the input string itself.", "tokens": [50515, 440, 15058, 4295, 307, 15957, 20458, 14819, 538, 264, 4846, 6798, 2564, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 150574, "start": 1512.6200000000001, "end": 1514.76, "text": " Fliction calls this selection determinism.", "tokens": [50709, 3235, 4105, 5498, 341, 9450, 15957, 1434, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 150574, "start": 1515.04, "end": 1519.42, "text": " Yes, but Fliction is also extremely precise about what this guarantees and what it doesn't.", "tokens": [50830, 1079, 11, 457, 3235, 4105, 307, 611, 4664, 13600, 466, 437, 341, 32567, 293, 437, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 150574, "start": 1519.9, "end": 1525.2, "text": " Selection determinism guarantees that the tools will be fetched, injected, and executed in the specified sequence.", "tokens": [51073, 1100, 5450, 15957, 1434, 32567, 300, 264, 3873, 486, 312, 23673, 292, 11, 36967, 11, 293, 17577, 294, 264, 22206, 8310, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 150574, "start": 1525.6, "end": 1528.32, "text": " It provides absolute architectural reliability.", "tokens": [51358, 467, 6417, 8236, 26621, 24550, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 150574, "start": 1528.74, "end": 1532.36, "text": " But wait, does explicit naming mean the skills will flawlessly work together?", "tokens": [51515, 583, 1699, 11, 775, 13691, 25290, 914, 264, 3942, 486, 13717, 12048, 589, 1214, 30, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980268697823044, "compression_ratio": 1.7074829931972788, "no_speech_prob": 2.2894490123159805e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 153236, "start": 1532.36, "end": 1535.6399999999999, "text": " What's fascinating here is it doesn't eliminate all risk.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 309, 1177, 380, 13819, 439, 3148, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 153236, "start": 1535.9799999999998, "end": 1541.76, "text": " The paper notes you still have network unavailability, conflicting instructions, or security risks in fetched text.", "tokens": [50546, 440, 3035, 5570, 291, 920, 362, 3209, 36541, 864, 2310, 11, 43784, 9415, 11, 420, 3825, 10888, 294, 23673, 292, 2487, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 153236, "start": 1542.1399999999999, "end": 1544.08, "text": " But it eliminates selection risk.", "tokens": [50854, 583, 309, 49893, 9450, 3148, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 153236, "start": 1544.58, "end": 1547.2199999999998, "text": " The skills will co-fire because you named them.", "tokens": [50976, 440, 3942, 486, 598, 12, 12037, 570, 291, 4926, 552, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 153236, "start": 1547.36, "end": 1547.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51115, 1779, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 153236, "start": 1547.78, "end": 1549.6, "text": " It does not guarantee semantic success.", "tokens": [51136, 467, 775, 406, 10815, 47982, 2245, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16247003142898148, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903572283901493e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 154960, "start": 1549.6, "end": 1559.08, "text": " If the static analysis tool downloads a corrupted binary, or if the LLM hallucinates the rejects pattern it feeds into the search tool, the pipeline still fails.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 13437, 5215, 2290, 36553, 257, 39480, 17434, 11, 420, 498, 264, 441, 43, 44, 35212, 259, 1024, 264, 8248, 82, 5102, 309, 23712, 666, 264, 3164, 2290, 11, 264, 15517, 920, 18199, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08531762392092974, "compression_ratio": 1.6105769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970322495688973e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 154960, "start": 1559.8799999999999, "end": 1564.62, "text": " Explicitly naming the paths guarantees that the agent walks into the operating room with the right scalpels.", "tokens": [50879, 2111, 4770, 270, 356, 25290, 264, 14518, 32567, 300, 264, 9461, 12896, 666, 264, 7447, 1808, 365, 264, 558, 31972, 1625, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08531762392092974, "compression_ratio": 1.6105769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970322495688973e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 154960, "start": 1564.84, "end": 1567.2199999999998, "text": " It doesn't guarantee the agent knows how to perform the surgery.", "tokens": [51127, 467, 1177, 380, 10815, 264, 9461, 3255, 577, 281, 2042, 264, 7930, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08531762392092974, "compression_ratio": 1.6105769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970322495688973e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 156722, "start": 1567.22, "end": 1568.14, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24475802650934533, "compression_ratio": 1.5727272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537873059526477e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 156722, "start": 1568.74, "end": 1572.34, "text": " You have mathematically isolated the selection risk from the execution risk.", "tokens": [50441, 509, 362, 44003, 14621, 264, 9450, 3148, 490, 264, 15058, 3148, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24475802650934533, "compression_ratio": 1.5727272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537873059526477e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 156722, "start": 1572.9, "end": 1581.6200000000001, "text": " But this entire residency analysis so far has been predicated on the assumption that the agent is using its internal attention mechanism, its prompt-to-managed state.", "tokens": [50649, 583, 341, 2302, 34014, 5215, 370, 1400, 575, 668, 3852, 3587, 322, 264, 15302, 300, 264, 9461, 307, 1228, 1080, 6920, 3202, 7513, 11, 1080, 12391, 12, 1353, 12, 1601, 2980, 1785, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24475802650934533, "compression_ratio": 1.5727272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537873059526477e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 156722, "start": 1582.28, "end": 1584.66, "text": " What happens if we change the architecture entirely?", "tokens": [51118, 708, 2314, 498, 321, 1319, 264, 9482, 7696, 30, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24475802650934533, "compression_ratio": 1.5727272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537873059526477e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 156722, "start": 1585.14, "end": 1586.94, "text": " If we rip the memory out of the agent?", "tokens": [51261, 759, 321, 12782, 264, 4675, 484, 295, 264, 9461, 30, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24475802650934533, "compression_ratio": 1.5727272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537873059526477e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 158694, "start": 1586.94, "end": 1589.44, "text": " This is exactly where my mind goes next.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 2293, 689, 452, 1575, 1709, 958, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15925834534016062, "compression_ratio": 1.5018181818181817, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682300072595746e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 158694, "start": 1589.94, "end": 1598.76, "text": " Because if this type theory framework is truly a universal law of software design, it cannot be uniquely bound to the specific quirks of Transformer Context Windows.", "tokens": [50515, 1436, 498, 341, 2010, 5261, 8388, 307, 4908, 257, 11455, 2101, 295, 4722, 1715, 11, 309, 2644, 312, 31474, 5472, 281, 264, 2685, 35645, 1694, 295, 27938, 260, 4839, 3828, 8591, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15925834534016062, "compression_ratio": 1.5018181818181817, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682300072595746e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 158694, "start": 1599.2, "end": 1601.92, "text": " It has to apply to fundamentally different architectures.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 575, 281, 3079, 281, 17879, 819, 6331, 1303, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15925834534016062, "compression_ratio": 1.5018181818181817, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682300072595746e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 158694, "start": 1602.54, "end": 1606.88, "text": " What happens when we implement a Retrieval Augmented Generation, or AN, R architecture?", "tokens": [51145, 708, 2314, 562, 321, 4445, 257, 11495, 5469, 3337, 6088, 14684, 23898, 11, 420, 5252, 11, 497, 9482, 30, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15925834534016062, "compression_ratio": 1.5018181818181817, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682300072595746e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 158694, "start": 1607.54, "end": 1610.8200000000002, "text": " In our AN pipeline, you utilize an external vector database.", "tokens": [51395, 682, 527, 5252, 15517, 11, 291, 16117, 364, 8320, 8062, 8149, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15925834534016062, "compression_ratio": 1.5018181818181817, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682300072595746e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 161082, "start": 1610.82, "end": 1621.22, "text": " Instead of forcing the LLM to hold the metadata of all 56,000 skills in its fragile 100-slot prompt, you compute vector embeddings for every skill and store them on a remote server.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 295, 19030, 264, 441, 43, 44, 281, 1797, 264, 26603, 295, 439, 19687, 11, 1360, 3942, 294, 1080, 23847, 2319, 12, 10418, 310, 12391, 11, 291, 14722, 8062, 12240, 29432, 337, 633, 5389, 293, 3531, 552, 322, 257, 8607, 7154, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09044563260852781, "compression_ratio": 1.6146496815286624, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492816448151037e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 161082, "start": 1621.34, "end": 1622.28, "text": " Right, a vector store.", "tokens": [50891, 1779, 11, 257, 8062, 3531, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09044563260852781, "compression_ratio": 1.6146496815286624, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492816448151037e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 161082, "start": 1622.4399999999998, "end": 1622.6, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50946, 865, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09044563260852781, "compression_ratio": 1.6146496815286624, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492816448151037e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 161082, "start": 1623.02, "end": 1635.1399999999999, "text": " When a user submits a prompt, a separate orchestration layer performs a cosine similarity search against that database, extracts the top three most semantically relevant skills, and injects only those into the prompt just before inference.", "tokens": [50975, 1133, 257, 4195, 8286, 1208, 257, 12391, 11, 257, 4994, 14161, 2405, 4583, 26213, 257, 23565, 32194, 3164, 1970, 300, 8149, 11, 8947, 82, 264, 1192, 1045, 881, 4361, 49505, 7340, 3942, 11, 293, 10711, 82, 787, 729, 666, 264, 12391, 445, 949, 38253, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09044563260852781, "compression_ratio": 1.6146496815286624, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492816448151037e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 161082, "start": 1635.5, "end": 1638.8, "text": " So the agent's baseline prompt remains completely empty.", "tokens": [51599, 407, 264, 9461, 311, 20518, 12391, 7023, 2584, 6707, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09044563260852781, "compression_ratio": 1.6146496815286624, "no_speech_prob": 1.5492816448151037e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 163880, "start": 1638.8, "end": 1643.1599999999999, "text": " It relies entirely on the external database to act as an omniscient librarian.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 30910, 7696, 322, 264, 8320, 8149, 281, 605, 382, 364, 3406, 10661, 5412, 42558, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 163880, "start": 1644.1399999999999, "end": 1649.2, "text": " In this RAG setup, does the trigger operation still map to the sort function?", "tokens": [50632, 682, 341, 14626, 38, 8657, 11, 775, 264, 7875, 6916, 920, 4471, 281, 264, 1333, 2445, 30, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 163880, "start": 1649.56, "end": 1652.3, "text": " Does it still demand the residency hypothesis?", "tokens": [50903, 4402, 309, 920, 4733, 264, 34014, 17291, 30, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 163880, "start": 1653.24, "end": 1656.96, "text": " No, because residency is no longer the governing structural relation.", "tokens": [51087, 883, 11, 570, 34014, 307, 572, 2854, 264, 30054, 15067, 9721, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 163880, "start": 1657.68, "end": 1663.3999999999999, "text": " In a retrieval-mediated architecture, Fliction points out that trigger fundamentally changes its mathematical mapping.", "tokens": [51309, 682, 257, 19817, 3337, 12, 3130, 770, 9482, 11, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 7875, 17879, 2962, 1080, 18894, 18350, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 163880, "start": 1663.86, "end": 1665.34, "text": " It no longer behaves like sort.", "tokens": [51618, 467, 572, 2854, 36896, 411, 1333, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 163880, "start": 1665.62, "end": 1666.74, "text": " It behaves like filter.", "tokens": [51706, 467, 36896, 411, 6608, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 163880, "start": 1667.02, "end": 1667.84, "text": " Let's unpack that.", "tokens": [51776, 961, 311, 26699, 300, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14366203273108247, "compression_ratio": 1.6443661971830985, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111113737201423e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 166784, "start": 1667.84, "end": 1675.02, "text": " The filter function takes a list and a predicate, a true-false condition, and returns a new list containing only the elements that satisfy that predicate.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 6608, 2445, 2516, 257, 1329, 293, 257, 3852, 8700, 11, 257, 2074, 12, 36474, 405, 4188, 11, 293, 11247, 257, 777, 1329, 19273, 787, 264, 4959, 300, 19319, 300, 3852, 8700, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 166784, "start": 1675.1799999999998, "end": 1675.6999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50732, 7587, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 166784, "start": 1676.06, "end": 1679.36, "text": " And the vector database is basically acting as a massive filter operation.", "tokens": [50776, 400, 264, 8062, 8149, 307, 1936, 6577, 382, 257, 5994, 6608, 6916, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 166784, "start": 1680.0, "end": 1683.4199999999998, "text": " The predicate is the relevant score generated by the similarity search.", "tokens": [50973, 440, 3852, 8700, 307, 264, 7340, 6175, 10833, 538, 264, 32194, 3164, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 166784, "start": 1683.78, "end": 1686.6999999999998, "text": " If the score is above a certain threshold, the skill is injected.", "tokens": [51162, 759, 264, 6175, 307, 3673, 257, 1629, 14678, 11, 264, 5389, 307, 36967, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 166784, "start": 1686.84, "end": 1688.1399999999999, "text": " If not, it is ignored.", "tokens": [51315, 759, 406, 11, 309, 307, 19735, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1051770846048991, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211958854707055e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 168814, "start": 1688.14, "end": 1688.8200000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2062113388724949, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.654893453176265e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 168814, "start": 1688.8200000000002, "end": 1693.94, "text": " And Wadler's theorem for filter requires a different hypothesis than sort.", "tokens": [50399, 400, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 20904, 337, 6608, 7029, 257, 819, 17291, 813, 1333, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2062113388724949, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.654893453176265e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 168814, "start": 1694.3200000000002, "end": 1699.2800000000002, "text": " For filter to commute across a transformation, it doesn't require residency or ordering.", "tokens": [50674, 1171, 6608, 281, 36750, 2108, 257, 9887, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 3651, 34014, 420, 21739, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2062113388724949, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.654893453176265e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 168814, "start": 1699.66, "end": 1702.0200000000002, "text": " It requires what is known as predicate transport.", "tokens": [50941, 467, 7029, 437, 307, 2570, 382, 3852, 8700, 5495, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2062113388724949, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.654893453176265e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 168814, "start": 1702.5800000000002, "end": 1707.44, "text": " The transformation must perfectly preserve the underlying logic of the predicate itself.", "tokens": [51087, 440, 9887, 1633, 6239, 15665, 264, 14217, 9952, 295, 264, 3852, 8700, 2564, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2062113388724949, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.654893453176265e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 170744, "start": 1707.44, "end": 1710.96, "text": " We have to translate that out of pure math and into database engineering.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 281, 13799, 300, 484, 295, 6075, 5221, 293, 666, 8149, 7043, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386894803298147, "compression_ratio": 1.353846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359729527297254e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 170744, "start": 1711.3600000000001, "end": 1716.6200000000001, "text": " What does predicate transport actually mean for a vector store managing thousands of skill embeddings?", "tokens": [50561, 708, 775, 3852, 8700, 5495, 767, 914, 337, 257, 8062, 3531, 11642, 5383, 295, 5389, 12240, 29432, 30, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386894803298147, "compression_ratio": 1.353846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359729527297254e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 171662, "start": 1716.62, "end": 1718.4799999999998, "text": " It means index consistency.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 8186, 14416, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 171662, "start": 1719.2199999999998, "end": 1728.7399999999998, "text": " In a RAG system, the vector embedding stored in the database is essentially a frozen mathematical representation of the skill.md file at the exact moment it was ingested.", "tokens": [50495, 682, 257, 14626, 38, 1185, 11, 264, 8062, 12240, 3584, 12187, 294, 264, 8149, 307, 4476, 257, 12496, 18894, 10290, 295, 264, 5389, 13, 76, 67, 3991, 412, 264, 1900, 1623, 309, 390, 3957, 21885, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 171662, "start": 1728.8, "end": 1730.06, "text": " Right. A snapshot in time.", "tokens": [50974, 1779, 13, 316, 30163, 294, 565, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 171662, "start": 1730.1399999999999, "end": 1730.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51041, 1779, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 171662, "start": 1730.86, "end": 1735.1999999999998, "text": " But what happens if a developer updates the underlying markdown file on disk?", "tokens": [51077, 583, 437, 2314, 498, 257, 10754, 9205, 264, 14217, 1491, 5093, 3991, 322, 12355, 30, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 171662, "start": 1735.34, "end": 1738.62, "text": " Oh, this is the exact real-world symptom the paper mentions.", "tokens": [51301, 876, 11, 341, 307, 264, 1900, 957, 12, 13217, 29370, 264, 3035, 23844, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 171662, "start": 1738.9599999999998, "end": 1739.56, "text": " Indexed illness.", "tokens": [51482, 33552, 292, 10152, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13202202922165995, "compression_ratio": 1.545816733067729, "no_speech_prob": 1.8181976106992903e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 173956, "start": 1739.56, "end": 1743.86, "text": " This is the classic agitizing edge case of every RAG system I've ever deployed.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 7230, 623, 270, 3319, 4691, 1389, 295, 633, 14626, 38, 1185, 286, 600, 1562, 17826, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 173956, "start": 1744.1, "end": 1745.06, "text": " It happens constantly.", "tokens": [50592, 467, 2314, 6460, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 173956, "start": 1745.3799999999999, "end": 1745.78, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50656, 467, 775, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 173956, "start": 1746.3, "end": 1748.98, "text": " Let's say my team updates our internal deployment script.", "tokens": [50702, 961, 311, 584, 452, 1469, 9205, 527, 6920, 19317, 5755, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 173956, "start": 1749.34, "end": 1751.82, "text": " We modify the school.md to say, crucial update.", "tokens": [50854, 492, 16927, 264, 1395, 13, 76, 67, 281, 584, 11, 11462, 5623, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 173956, "start": 1752.26, "end": 1755.3, "text": " Do not use the legacy v1 endpoint under any circumstances.", "tokens": [51000, 1144, 406, 764, 264, 11711, 371, 16, 35795, 833, 604, 9121, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 173956, "start": 1755.8, "end": 1756.72, "text": " Only reap to v2.", "tokens": [51177, 5686, 39178, 281, 371, 17, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 173956, "start": 1757.3799999999999, "end": 1759.32, "text": " The file on the hard drive is updated perfectly.", "tokens": [51256, 440, 3991, 322, 264, 1152, 3332, 307, 10588, 6239, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 173956, "start": 1759.8, "end": 1763.6599999999999, "text": " But if you fail to explicitly trigger a re-indexing pipeline,", "tokens": [51377, 583, 498, 291, 3061, 281, 20803, 7875, 257, 319, 12, 471, 3121, 278, 15517, 11, 51570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 173956, "start": 1763.98, "end": 1768.12, "text": " if you don't recalculate the vector embeddings and push them to the external database,", "tokens": [51586, 498, 291, 500, 380, 850, 304, 2444, 473, 264, 8062, 12240, 29432, 293, 2944, 552, 281, 264, 8320, 8149, 11, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1642272807933666, "compression_ratio": 1.5587301587301587, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554037650552301e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 176812, "start": 1768.12, "end": 1770.08, "text": " what happens to the predicate?", "tokens": [50365, 437, 2314, 281, 264, 3852, 8700, 30, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 176812, "start": 1770.32, "end": 1772.12, "text": " The predicate is operating on ghost data.", "tokens": [50475, 440, 3852, 8700, 307, 7447, 322, 8359, 1412, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 176812, "start": 1772.5, "end": 1776.34, "text": " The vector database still thinks the skill is fundamentally about the legacy v1 endpoint.", "tokens": [50584, 440, 8062, 8149, 920, 7309, 264, 5389, 307, 17879, 466, 264, 11711, 371, 16, 35795, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 176812, "start": 1776.62, "end": 1780.08, "text": " The predicate hasn't transported across the representational change on disk.", "tokens": [50790, 440, 3852, 8700, 6132, 380, 29373, 2108, 264, 2906, 1478, 1319, 322, 12355, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 176812, "start": 1780.4199999999998, "end": 1781.7399999999998, "text": " We've induced index staleness.", "tokens": [50980, 492, 600, 33991, 8186, 49875, 15264, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 176812, "start": 1782.4199999999998, "end": 1785.08, "text": " So when a user asks the agent to execute a v2 deployment,", "tokens": [51080, 407, 562, 257, 4195, 8962, 264, 9461, 281, 14483, 257, 371, 17, 19317, 11, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 176812, "start": 1785.58, "end": 1789.8799999999999, "text": " the vector database calculates a low relevant score because its embedded predicate is outdated.", "tokens": [51238, 264, 8062, 8149, 4322, 1024, 257, 2295, 7340, 6175, 570, 1080, 16741, 3852, 8700, 307, 36313, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 176812, "start": 1790.26, "end": 1791.9199999999998, "text": " It silently filters this skill out.", "tokens": [51472, 467, 40087, 15995, 341, 5389, 484, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 176812, "start": 1792.3999999999999, "end": 1793.08, "text": " The agent fails.", "tokens": [51579, 440, 9461, 18199, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 176812, "start": 1793.08, "end": 1797.76, "text": " This proves that migrating to a RAG architecture does not eliminate the preservation obligation.", "tokens": [51613, 639, 25019, 300, 6186, 8754, 281, 257, 14626, 38, 9482, 775, 406, 13819, 264, 27257, 20326, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17396686326211958, "compression_ratio": 1.7237237237237237, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928132053206095e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 179776, "start": 1797.76, "end": 1799.3799999999999, "text": " It merely migrates it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 17003, 6186, 12507, 309, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 179776, "start": 1799.64, "end": 1800.8, "text": " That is so wild.", "tokens": [50459, 663, 307, 370, 4868, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 179776, "start": 1801.16, "end": 1801.64, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50535, 467, 307, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 179776, "start": 1801.96, "end": 1805.0, "text": " When you rely on a prompt mediated architecture,", "tokens": [50575, 1133, 291, 10687, 322, 257, 12391, 17269, 770, 9482, 11, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 179776, "start": 1805.74, "end": 1807.76, "text": " auto-triggering demands residency preservation.", "tokens": [50764, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 15107, 34014, 27257, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 179776, "start": 1808.6, "end": 1811.3, "text": " You pay a standing token tax to maintain that structure.", "tokens": [50907, 509, 1689, 257, 4877, 14862, 3366, 281, 6909, 300, 3877, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 179776, "start": 1811.78, "end": 1814.52, "text": " When you switch to a retrieval mediated architecture,", "tokens": [51066, 1133, 291, 3679, 281, 257, 19817, 3337, 17269, 770, 9482, 11, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 179776, "start": 1815.02, "end": 1817.18, "text": " auto-triggering demands index consistency.", "tokens": [51228, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 15107, 8186, 14416, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 179776, "start": 1818.0, "end": 1822.86, "text": " You trade a standing token tax for a continuous, highly complex synchronization obligation.", "tokens": [51377, 509, 4923, 257, 4877, 14862, 3366, 337, 257, 10957, 11, 5405, 3997, 19331, 2144, 20326, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22040342330932616, "compression_ratio": 1.7762557077625571, "no_speech_prob": 2.6244321386231784e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 182286, "start": 1822.86, "end": 1828.62, "text": " You escape the LLM memory bottleneck only to inherit a distributed systems engineering nightmare.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 7615, 264, 441, 43, 44, 4675, 44641, 547, 787, 281, 21389, 257, 12631, 3652, 7043, 18724, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16351422809419178, "compression_ratio": 1.4039408866995073, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760876099171986e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 182286, "start": 1829.5, "end": 1833.78, "text": " Both architectures demand heavy representational luggage to support the auto-triggering feature,", "tokens": [50697, 6767, 6331, 1303, 4733, 4676, 2906, 1478, 27744, 281, 1406, 264, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 4111, 11, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16351422809419178, "compression_ratio": 1.4039408866995073, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760876099171986e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 182286, "start": 1834.1, "end": 1838.24, "text": " which really highlights just how elegant Yin's Tier 1 bare reference truly is.", "tokens": [50927, 597, 534, 14254, 445, 577, 21117, 33254, 311, 24224, 502, 6949, 6408, 4908, 307, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16351422809419178, "compression_ratio": 1.4039408866995073, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760876099171986e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 182286, "start": 1838.32, "end": 1838.82, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [51138, 7021, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16351422809419178, "compression_ratio": 1.4039408866995073, "no_speech_prob": 1.8760876099171986e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 183882, "start": 1838.82, "end": 1843.02, "text": " By choosing to explicitly name the path and bypass auto-triggering entirely,", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 10875, 281, 20803, 1315, 264, 3100, 293, 24996, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 7696, 11, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18900761780915437, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686642463195746e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 183882, "start": 1843.5, "end": 1845.52, "text": " you remain in the territory of head and frest.", "tokens": [50599, 291, 6222, 294, 264, 11360, 295, 1378, 293, 2130, 372, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18900761780915437, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686642463195746e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 183882, "start": 1845.82, "end": 1850.52, "text": " You incur zero prompt residency tax, and you require zero vector synchronization pipelines.", "tokens": [50715, 509, 35774, 4018, 12391, 34014, 3366, 11, 293, 291, 3651, 4018, 8062, 19331, 2144, 40168, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18900761780915437, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686642463195746e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 183882, "start": 1850.8999999999999, "end": 1853.74, "text": " You're operating purely on the semantic identity of the content.", "tokens": [50969, 509, 434, 7447, 17491, 322, 264, 47982, 6575, 295, 264, 2701, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18900761780915437, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686642463195746e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 183882, "start": 1854.1399999999999, "end": 1858.0, "text": " And this realization leads to the grand synthesis of Fliction's paper.", "tokens": [51131, 400, 341, 25138, 6689, 281, 264, 2697, 30252, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 3035, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18900761780915437, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686642463195746e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 185800, "start": 1858.0, "end": 1861.26, "text": " Having traced the mechanisms of token exhaustion,", "tokens": [50365, 10222, 38141, 264, 15902, 295, 14862, 47408, 11, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 185800, "start": 1861.94, "end": 1865.16, "text": " mapped the AtSkills protocol to Wadler's free theorems,", "tokens": [50562, 33318, 264, 1711, 50, 74, 2565, 10336, 281, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 1737, 10299, 2592, 11, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 185800, "start": 1865.48, "end": 1868.3, "text": " and stress-tested the theory against vector databases,", "tokens": [50739, 293, 4244, 12, 83, 21885, 264, 5261, 1970, 8062, 22380, 11, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 185800, "start": 1868.98, "end": 1874.08, "text": " Fliction zooms all the way out to establish a broader framework for evaluating system architecture.", "tokens": [50914, 3235, 4105, 5721, 4785, 439, 264, 636, 484, 281, 8327, 257, 13227, 8388, 337, 27479, 1185, 9482, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 185800, "start": 1874.84, "end": 1880.66, "text": " Fliction formalizes this by defining two distinct types of invariants that govern every software operation.", "tokens": [51207, 3235, 4105, 9860, 5660, 341, 538, 17827, 732, 10644, 3467, 295, 33270, 1719, 300, 1980, 633, 4722, 6916, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 185800, "start": 1881.0, "end": 1884.1, "text": " This is where the paper transforms from an AI engineering critique", "tokens": [51515, 639, 307, 689, 264, 3035, 35592, 490, 364, 7318, 7043, 25673, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 185800, "start": 1884.1, "end": 1886.8, "text": " into a master class on software philosophy.", "tokens": [51670, 666, 257, 4505, 1508, 322, 4722, 10675, 13, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664396624698817, "compression_ratio": 1.5913621262458473, "no_speech_prob": 1.920402422153633e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 188680, "start": 1886.8, "end": 1889.0, "text": " Let's break down these two invariants.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 613, 732, 33270, 1719, 13, 50475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 188680, "start": 1889.2, "end": 1889.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50485, 1779, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 188680, "start": 1889.48, "end": 1893.12, "text": " The first is what Fliction labels Fliction, which stands for semantic obligations.", "tokens": [50499, 440, 700, 307, 437, 3235, 4105, 16949, 3235, 4105, 11, 597, 7382, 337, 47982, 26234, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 188680, "start": 1893.56, "end": 1893.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50703, 1779, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 188680, "start": 1894.24, "end": 1899.6, "text": " A semantic obligation is the bedrock requirement for an operation to retain its fundamental identity.", "tokens": [50737, 316, 47982, 20326, 307, 264, 2901, 17799, 11695, 337, 364, 6916, 281, 18340, 1080, 8088, 6575, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 188680, "start": 1899.86, "end": 1902.6599999999999, "text": " It's what must be preserved for an operation to remain itself.", "tokens": [51018, 467, 311, 437, 1633, 312, 22242, 337, 364, 6916, 281, 6222, 2564, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 188680, "start": 1903.1399999999999, "end": 1906.84, "text": " For our resolve operation, the act of fetching and reading a file,", "tokens": [51182, 1171, 527, 14151, 6916, 11, 264, 605, 295, 23673, 278, 293, 3760, 257, 3991, 11, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 188680, "start": 1907.04, "end": 1909.56, "text": " the Fliction is strictly bound to content identity.", "tokens": [51377, 264, 3235, 4105, 307, 20792, 5472, 281, 2701, 6575, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 188680, "start": 1910.02, "end": 1915.1599999999999, "text": " So if the hard drive corrupts and replaces the markdown file with randomly generated binary noise,", "tokens": [51526, 407, 498, 264, 1152, 3332, 17366, 82, 293, 46734, 264, 1491, 5093, 3991, 365, 16979, 10833, 17434, 5658, 11, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16008584867647993, "compression_ratio": 1.7862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129242460891316e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 191516, "start": 1915.16, "end": 1917.8200000000002, "text": " the resolve operation catastrophically fails.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 14151, 6916, 28363, 984, 18199, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 191516, "start": 1917.88, "end": 1919.1200000000001, "text": " It ceases to be resolved.", "tokens": [50501, 467, 1769, 1957, 281, 312, 20772, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 191516, "start": 1919.44, "end": 1919.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50579, 1779, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 191516, "start": 1919.9, "end": 1923.8600000000001, "text": " You cannot read a text file if the text itself has been digitally incinerated.", "tokens": [50602, 509, 2644, 1401, 257, 2487, 3991, 498, 264, 2487, 2564, 575, 668, 36938, 834, 4564, 770, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 191516, "start": 1924.3000000000002, "end": 1926.2, "text": " That is a semantic truth of computing.", "tokens": [50822, 663, 307, 257, 47982, 3494, 295, 15866, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 191516, "start": 1926.38, "end": 1926.9, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50926, 48746, 736, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 191516, "start": 1927.44, "end": 1931.74, "text": " Every operation, regardless of its design, carries an inescapable power one dollar.", "tokens": [50979, 2048, 6916, 11, 10060, 295, 1080, 1715, 11, 16402, 364, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 1347, 472, 7241, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 191516, "start": 1932.1200000000001, "end": 1933.8600000000001, "text": " But then we introduce the second invariant,", "tokens": [51213, 583, 550, 321, 5366, 264, 1150, 33270, 394, 11, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 191516, "start": 1934.24, "end": 1936.98, "text": " a PRE, which stands for representational obligations.", "tokens": [51319, 257, 44164, 11, 597, 7382, 337, 2906, 1478, 26234, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19572799984771427, "compression_ratio": 1.531496062992126, "no_speech_prob": 2.446247631543441e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 193698, "start": 1936.98, "end": 1944.26, "text": " This is the supplemental structural luggage that a specific implementation or feature set demands in order to execute successfully.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 48604, 15067, 27744, 300, 257, 2685, 11420, 420, 4111, 992, 15107, 294, 1668, 281, 14483, 10727, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15989322865262945, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.973640001429189e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 193698, "start": 1944.46, "end": 1949.92, "text": " This is the hypothesis we were talking about earlier, like reading a skill via a bare reference has an empty PREA.", "tokens": [50739, 639, 307, 264, 17291, 321, 645, 1417, 466, 3071, 11, 411, 3760, 257, 5389, 5766, 257, 6949, 6408, 575, 364, 6707, 44164, 32, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15989322865262945, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.973640001429189e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 193698, "start": 1950.06, "end": 1951.78, "text": " It demands zero extra structure.", "tokens": [51019, 467, 15107, 4018, 2857, 3877, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15989322865262945, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.973640001429189e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 193698, "start": 1952.54, "end": 1956.4, "text": " But auto-triggering a skill has a massive, complex power end.", "tokens": [51143, 583, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 257, 5389, 575, 257, 5994, 11, 3997, 1347, 917, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15989322865262945, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.973640001429189e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 193698, "start": 1956.96, "end": 1962.96, "text": " It demands either strict prompt residency or perfect index synchronization across a distributed database.", "tokens": [51364, 467, 15107, 2139, 10910, 12391, 34014, 420, 2176, 8186, 19331, 2144, 2108, 257, 12631, 8149, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15989322865262945, "compression_ratio": 1.6433823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.973640001429189e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 196296, "start": 1962.96, "end": 1967.96, "text": " This distinction allows Fliction to diagnose the root cause of the AI agent bottleneck.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 16844, 4045, 3235, 4105, 281, 36238, 264, 5593, 3082, 295, 264, 7318, 9461, 44641, 547, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 196296, "start": 1968.8400000000001, "end": 1971.1200000000001, "text": " The problem wasn't that LLMs are physically flawed.", "tokens": [50659, 440, 1154, 2067, 380, 300, 441, 43, 26386, 366, 9762, 38823, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 196296, "start": 1971.22, "end": 1973.3400000000001, "text": " The problem was the bundling pathology.", "tokens": [50778, 440, 1154, 390, 264, 13882, 1688, 3100, 1793, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 196296, "start": 1973.54, "end": 1974.32, "text": " The bundling pathology.", "tokens": [50894, 440, 13882, 1688, 3100, 1793, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 196296, "start": 1974.44, "end": 1974.54, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50939, 865, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 196296, "start": 1974.82, "end": 1977.96, "text": " This pathology infects a system when an architect takes multiple operations,", "tokens": [50958, 639, 3100, 1793, 5888, 82, 257, 1185, 562, 364, 6331, 2516, 3866, 7705, 11, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 196296, "start": 1978.74, "end": 1980.88, "text": " some with an empty PREA and some with a massive power,", "tokens": [51154, 512, 365, 364, 6707, 44164, 32, 293, 512, 365, 257, 5994, 1347, 11, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 196296, "start": 1981.02, "end": 1985.68, "text": " and irreversibly fuses them together behind a single, opaque user interface.", "tokens": [51268, 293, 16014, 840, 3545, 283, 8355, 552, 1214, 2261, 257, 2167, 11, 42687, 4195, 9226, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 196296, "start": 1985.8600000000001, "end": 1987.96, "text": " Like the ubiquitous install button.", "tokens": [51510, 1743, 264, 43868, 39831, 3625, 2960, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 196296, "start": 1988.1000000000001, "end": 1988.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51622, 7587, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16120479901631674, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.307053419831062e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 198848, "start": 1988.48, "end": 1993.56, "text": " When you bundle operations this way, you trigger what Fliction terms commitment leakage.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 24438, 7705, 341, 636, 11, 291, 7875, 437, 3235, 4105, 2115, 8371, 47799, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 198848, "start": 1994.3, "end": 2000.52, "text": " The massive representational obligations of the auto-trigger feature bleed out and contaminate the simple read feature.", "tokens": [50656, 440, 5994, 2906, 1478, 26234, 295, 264, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 4111, 28385, 484, 293, 27562, 473, 264, 2199, 1401, 4111, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 198848, "start": 2000.72, "end": 2004.32, "text": " And the pointer-level mechanism of this leakage is insidious.", "tokens": [50977, 400, 264, 23918, 12, 12418, 7513, 295, 341, 47799, 307, 1028, 327, 851, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 198848, "start": 2005.16, "end": 2007.56, "text": " Because the system only exposes the bundle,", "tokens": [51199, 1436, 264, 1185, 787, 1278, 4201, 264, 24438, 11, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 198848, "start": 2008.1200000000001, "end": 2012.54, "text": " the execution runtime is forced to allocate the memory, track the state,", "tokens": [51347, 264, 15058, 34474, 307, 7579, 281, 35713, 264, 4675, 11, 2837, 264, 1785, 11, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 198848, "start": 2012.76, "end": 2016.44, "text": " and maintain the structural hypotheses for all sub-operations.", "tokens": [51579, 293, 6909, 264, 15067, 49969, 337, 439, 1422, 12, 7192, 763, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529330546312993, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.2100281674153344e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 201644, "start": 2016.44, "end": 2019.96, "text": " Even if the user only intends to utilize the simplest one.", "tokens": [50365, 2754, 498, 264, 4195, 787, 560, 2581, 281, 16117, 264, 22811, 472, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 201644, "start": 2020.6000000000001, "end": 2023.7, "text": " So the operation's individual luggage is smaller than the bundle's luggage,", "tokens": [50573, 407, 264, 6916, 311, 2609, 27744, 307, 4356, 813, 264, 24438, 311, 27744, 11, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 201644, "start": 2024.04, "end": 2027.04, "text": " but the system forces you to carry the entire bundle anyway.", "tokens": [50745, 457, 264, 1185, 5874, 291, 281, 3985, 264, 2302, 24438, 4033, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 201644, "start": 2027.24, "end": 2029.02, "text": " It's economically disastrous at scale.", "tokens": [50905, 467, 311, 26811, 44502, 412, 4373, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 201644, "start": 2029.76, "end": 2033.8400000000001, "text": " The pathology becomes fatal because the system inherently prices the entire interface", "tokens": [51031, 440, 3100, 1793, 3643, 24069, 570, 264, 1185, 27993, 7901, 264, 2302, 9226, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 201644, "start": 2033.8400000000001, "end": 2036.3600000000001, "text": " at the rate of the most expensive internal operation.", "tokens": [51235, 412, 264, 3314, 295, 264, 881, 5124, 6920, 6916, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 201644, "start": 2036.9, "end": 2039.5800000000002, "text": " You are forced to pay the 50-token prompt tax,", "tokens": [51388, 509, 366, 7579, 281, 1689, 264, 2625, 12, 83, 8406, 12391, 3366, 11, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 201644, "start": 2039.8200000000002, "end": 2041.5, "text": " the heavy prep of the trigger operation,", "tokens": [51534, 264, 4676, 2666, 295, 264, 7875, 6916, 11, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 201644, "start": 2041.64, "end": 2044.22, "text": " for a skill that you only ever needed to resolve once.", "tokens": [51625, 337, 257, 5389, 300, 291, 787, 1562, 2978, 281, 14151, 1564, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14694512476686572, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.825495700782942e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 204422, "start": 2044.22, "end": 2046.66, "text": " It is a systemic design defect.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 23789, 1715, 16445, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 204422, "start": 2047.48, "end": 2051.16, "text": " It is not an unavoidable physical reality of artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50528, 467, 307, 406, 364, 36541, 17079, 712, 4001, 4103, 295, 11677, 7599, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 204422, "start": 2051.82, "end": 2055.52, "text": " It's a human failure to respect mathematical boundaries in software architecture.", "tokens": [50745, 467, 311, 257, 1952, 7763, 281, 3104, 18894, 13180, 294, 4722, 9482, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 204422, "start": 2056.06, "end": 2060.94, "text": " A well-designed system charges an operation only for its specific representational structure.", "tokens": [50957, 316, 731, 12, 14792, 16690, 1185, 12235, 364, 6916, 787, 337, 1080, 2685, 2906, 1478, 3877, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 204422, "start": 2061.02, "end": 2061.92, "text": " So what does this all mean?", "tokens": [51205, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 30, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 204422, "start": 2062.1, "end": 2064.46, "text": " Well, by unbundling the interface,", "tokens": [51259, 1042, 11, 538, 517, 65, 997, 1688, 264, 9226, 11, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 204422, "start": 2064.86, "end": 2067.02, "text": " Yin et al. cured the pathology.", "tokens": [51397, 33254, 1030, 419, 13, 29617, 264, 3100, 1793, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 204422, "start": 2067.44, "end": 2069.2200000000003, "text": " They physically severed the memory pointers", "tokens": [51526, 814, 9762, 2802, 292, 264, 4675, 44548, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13353641434471206, "compression_ratio": 1.5817490494296578, "no_speech_prob": 1.7619858480241724e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 206922, "start": 2069.22, "end": 2073.64, "text": " connecting the resolve execution path from the trigger state requirements.", "tokens": [50365, 11015, 264, 14151, 15058, 3100, 490, 264, 7875, 1785, 7728, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 206922, "start": 2074.3999999999996, "end": 2077.0, "text": " They allowed you to execute operations with an empty prep", "tokens": [50624, 814, 4350, 291, 281, 14483, 7705, 365, 364, 6707, 2666, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 206922, "start": 2077.0, "end": 2079.48, "text": " without paying the toll for the heavy prep features.", "tokens": [50754, 1553, 6229, 264, 16629, 337, 264, 4676, 2666, 4122, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 206922, "start": 2079.98, "end": 2083.64, "text": " Infliction beautifully terms this cured state commitment honesty.", "tokens": [50903, 682, 3423, 4105, 16525, 2115, 341, 29617, 1785, 8371, 26839, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 206922, "start": 2084.64, "end": 2088.24, "text": " A commitment honest system is one where the architectural cost of an operation", "tokens": [51136, 316, 8371, 3245, 1185, 307, 472, 689, 264, 26621, 2063, 295, 364, 6916, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 206922, "start": 2088.24, "end": 2091.72, "text": " is strictly proportional to its inherent representational obligations", "tokens": [51316, 307, 20792, 24969, 281, 1080, 26387, 2906, 1478, 26234, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 206922, "start": 2091.72, "end": 2093.6, "text": " and absolutely nothing else.", "tokens": [51490, 293, 3122, 1825, 1646, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 206922, "start": 2093.9199999999996, "end": 2097.66, "text": " It refuses to charge you for the structural assumptions of features you aren't invoking.", "tokens": [51600, 467, 33222, 281, 4602, 291, 337, 264, 15067, 17695, 295, 4122, 291, 3212, 380, 1048, 5953, 13, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852500878847563, "compression_ratio": 1.7800687285223367, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325103603329836e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 209766, "start": 2097.66, "end": 2099.08, "text": " Commitment honesty.", "tokens": [50365, 3046, 270, 518, 26839, 13, 50436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 209766, "start": 2099.08, "end": 2103.04, "text": " I want to highlight that phrase because it is an incredibly powerful lens", "tokens": [50436, 286, 528, 281, 5078, 300, 9535, 570, 309, 307, 364, 6252, 4005, 6765, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 209766, "start": 2103.04, "end": 2106.44, "text": " through which to view not just AI but all software engineering.", "tokens": [50634, 807, 597, 281, 1910, 406, 445, 7318, 457, 439, 4722, 7043, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 209766, "start": 2107.3199999999997, "end": 2111.68, "text": " This paper proves that forcing operations with no representational commitment", "tokens": [50848, 639, 3035, 25019, 300, 19030, 7705, 365, 572, 2906, 1478, 8371, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 209766, "start": 2111.68, "end": 2114.16, "text": " to pay the cost of operations that do have them", "tokens": [51066, 281, 1689, 264, 2063, 295, 7705, 300, 360, 362, 552, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 209766, "start": 2114.16, "end": 2117.6, "text": " is a design defect, not a physical necessity of AI.", "tokens": [51190, 307, 257, 1715, 16445, 11, 406, 257, 4001, 24217, 295, 7318, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 209766, "start": 2118.54, "end": 2121.12, "text": " Let's briefly recap the arc of this deep dive.", "tokens": [51409, 961, 311, 10515, 20928, 264, 10346, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442993799845377, "compression_ratio": 1.5591836734693878, "no_speech_prob": 3.517627595456263e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 212112, "start": 2121.12, "end": 2126.12, "text": " We started with the very real immediate crisis of AI agents silently failing", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 588, 957, 11629, 5869, 295, 7318, 12554, 40087, 18223, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 212112, "start": 2126.12, "end": 2129.3399999999997, "text": " because their 100-slot attention mechanisms were being suffocated", "tokens": [50615, 570, 641, 2319, 12, 10418, 310, 3202, 15902, 645, 885, 3889, 905, 770, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 212112, "start": 2129.3399999999997, "end": 2131.8199999999997, "text": " by tens of thousands of installed skills.", "tokens": [50776, 538, 10688, 295, 5383, 295, 8899, 3942, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 212112, "start": 2132.16, "end": 2135.52, "text": " And then we examined the empirical solution provided by the AtSkills protocol", "tokens": [50917, 400, 550, 321, 30972, 264, 31886, 3827, 5649, 538, 264, 1711, 50, 74, 2565, 10336, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 212112, "start": 2135.52, "end": 2138.66, "text": " which unbundled installation into three isolated tiers", "tokens": [51085, 597, 517, 65, 997, 1493, 13260, 666, 1045, 14621, 40563, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 212112, "start": 2138.66, "end": 2140.5, "text": " reading, saving, and auto-triggering", "tokens": [51242, 3760, 11, 6816, 11, 293, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 212112, "start": 2140.5, "end": 2143.8399999999997, "text": " proving that only the auto-triggering feature physically required", "tokens": [51334, 27221, 300, 787, 264, 8399, 12, 6903, 6812, 278, 4111, 9762, 4739, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 212112, "start": 2143.8399999999997, "end": 2145.72, "text": " a token footprint in the active prompt.", "tokens": [51501, 257, 14862, 24222, 294, 264, 4967, 12391, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10095926088707469, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 3.265432629157017e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 214572, "start": 2145.72, "end": 2150.7, "text": " We then used Wadler's 1989 free theorems to prove why this unbundling worked", "tokens": [50365, 492, 550, 1143, 343, 345, 1918, 311, 22427, 1737, 10299, 2592, 281, 7081, 983, 341, 517, 65, 997, 1688, 2732, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1248944469333924, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678817615217723e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 214572, "start": 2150.7, "end": 2151.7599999999998, "text": " at a mathematical level.", "tokens": [50614, 412, 257, 18894, 1496, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1248944469333924, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678817615217723e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 214572, "start": 2152.54, "end": 2155.2799999999997, "text": " We mapped the zero-cost resolve and save operations", "tokens": [50706, 492, 33318, 264, 4018, 12, 27718, 14151, 293, 3155, 7705, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1248944469333924, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678817615217723e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 214572, "start": 2155.2799999999997, "end": 2158.54, "text": " to genuinely parametric functions like head and fast", "tokens